window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 16 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074681","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, select the related word from the given alternatives.<br><b>Sheep : fold :: pig : ?</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दिए गए विकल्पों में से संबंधित शब्द चुनिए।<br><b>भेड़ : बाड़ा :: सूअर : ?</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Den"},"2":{"en":"Sheet"},"3":{"en":"Sty"},"4":{"en":"Kennel"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A ‘fold’ is the enclosure in which sheep are kept.<br>In the same way, a ‘sty’ is the enclosure in which pigs are kept.<br>(Den – shelter of a wild animal, sheet – a piece of cloth, kennel – house of a dog)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Sty.</b>","hi":"‘फोल्ड’ (fold) वह बाड़ा है जिसमें भेड़ें रखी जाती हैं।<br>उसी प्रकार ‘स्टाय’ (sty) वह बाड़ा है जिसमें सूअर रखे जाते हैं।<br>(डेन – जंगली जानवर की मांद, शीट – कपड़े का टुकड़ा, केनल – कुत्ते का घर)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): Sty है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074682","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If + = ×, − = ÷, × = +, ÷ = −, then <b>64 − 4 + 2 × 6 = ?</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि + = ×, − = ÷, × = +, ÷ = − है, तो <b>64 − 4 + 2 × 6 = ?</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"38"},"2":{"en":"67"},"3":{"en":"34"},"4":{"en":"71"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Replacing the signs as given:<br>64 − 4 + 2 × 6 → 64 ÷ 4 × 2 + 6<br>64 ÷ 4 = 16<br>16 × 2 = 32<br>32 + 6 = 38<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 38.</b>","hi":"दिए गए नियम के अनुसार चिह्न बदलने पर:<br>64 − 4 + 2 × 6 → 64 ÷ 4 × 2 + 6<br>64 ÷ 4 = 16<br>16 × 2 = 32<br>32 + 6 = 38<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 38 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074683","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Solve the equation. What is 5 multiplied by (12 − 7)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"समीकरण हल कीजिए। 5 को (12 − 7) से गुणा करने पर क्या प्राप्त होगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35"},"2":{"en":"25"},"3":{"en":"30"},"4":{"en":"20"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"First solve the bracket:<br>(12 − 7) = 5<br>5 × 5 = 25<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 25.</b>","hi":"पहले कोष्ठक को हल कीजिए:<br>(12 − 7) = 5<br>5 × 5 = 25<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074684","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Evaluate: 5<sup>3</sup> ÷ 25 + 4<sup>2</sup> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: 5<sup>3</sup> ÷ 25 + 4<sup>2</sup> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"17"},"2":{"en":"19"},"3":{"en":"23"},"4":{"en":"21"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"5<sup>3</sup> = 125 and 4<sup>2</sup> = 16<br>125 ÷ 25 = 5<br>5 + 16 = 21<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 21.</b>","hi":"5<sup>3</sup> = 125 तथा 4<sup>2</sup> = 16<br>125 ÷ 25 = 5<br>5 + 16 = 21<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 21 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074685","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dictionary / Alphabetical Order","question":{"en":"Which of the following words comes first in a dictionary? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा शब्द शब्दकोश में सबसे पहले आता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Festival"},"2":{"en":"Fiction"},"3":{"en":"Fellow"},"4":{"en":"Fidelity"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The first two letters of every option are the same, so the third letter decides the order.<br>Fe-l-l-ow, Fe-s-t-ival, Fi-c-tion, Fi-d-elity.<br>As ‘e’ comes before ‘i’ and l comes before s, the order is: Fellow → Festival → Fiction → Fidelity.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Fellow.</b>","hi":"सभी विकल्पों के पहले दो अक्षर समान हैं, इसलिए तीसरा अक्षर क्रम तय करेगा।<br>Fe-l-l-ow, Fe-s-t-ival, Fi-c-tion, Fi-d-elity<br>‘e’, ‘i’ से पहले आता है और l, s से पहले आता है, इसलिए क्रम है: Fellow → Festival → Fiction → Fidelity<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): Fellow है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074686","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"If every bird can fly except ostriches, what can be concluded if an animal is an ostrich? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि शुतुरमुर्ग को छोड़कर हर पक्षी उड़ सकता है, तो यदि कोई जानवर शुतुरमुर्ग है तो क्या निष्कर्ष निकाला जा सकता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It can fly","hi":"वह उड़ सकता है"},"2":{"en":"It cannot fly","hi":"वह उड़ नहीं सकता"},"3":{"en":"It may or may not fly","hi":"वह उड़ सकता भी है और नहीं भी"},"4":{"en":"It flies occasionally","hi":"वह कभी-कभी उड़ता है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"An ostrich is a bird, but the given statement keeps ostriches out of the group of birds that can fly.<br>Therefore an ostrich cannot fly.<br>The options ‘may or may not fly’ and ‘flies occasionally’ go against the given statement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): It cannot fly.</b>","hi":"शुतुरमुर्ग एक पक्षी है, किंतु दिया गया कथन शुतुरमुर्ग को उड़ने वाले पक्षियों के समूह से बाहर रखता है।<br>इसलिए शुतुरमुर्ग उड़ नहीं सकता।<br>‘उड़ सकता भी है और नहीं भी’ तथा ‘कभी-कभी उड़ता है’ विकल्प दिए गए कथन के विरुद्ध हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): वह उड़ नहीं सकता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074687","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"From the options in Image Y, select the figure that finishes the analogy in Image X logically.<br>Image X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197c011-79ca-77e3-90ae-c9cd4b26d018_EN.jpg?edu=639294378590706735\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"छवि Y में दिए गए विकल्पों में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो छवि X में दिए गए सादृश्य को तार्किक रूप से पूरा करती है।<br>छवि X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197c011-79ca-77e3-90ae-c9cd4b26d018_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725415302\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In Image X, the second figure is obtained by turning the first figure through 180°, so that the arrow and the dot take exactly opposite positions.<br>In the third figure a square contains a small arrow; on turning it through 180° in the same manner the arrow must point in the opposite direction and sit on the opposite side of the square.<br>Among the figures of Image Y this is figure (1).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"छवि X में दूसरी आकृति पहली आकृति को 180° घुमाने पर प्राप्त होती है, जिससे तीर और बिंदु ठीक विपरीत स्थिति में आ जाते हैं।<br>तीसरी आकृति में एक वर्ग के भीतर छोटा तीर है; उसे भी उसी प्रकार 180° घुमाने पर तीर विपरीत दिशा में तथा वर्ग के विपरीत भाग में होना चाहिए।<br>छवि Y में यह आकृति (1) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197c011-79ca-77e3-90ae-c9cd4b26d018_EN.jpg?edu=639294378590706735","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197c011-79ca-77e3-90ae-c9cd4b26d018_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725415302"]}},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074688","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If ⊕ means multiply and ⊖ means subtract, what is 7 ⊕ 3 ⊖ 2? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि ⊕ का अर्थ गुणा है और ⊖ का अर्थ घटाना है, तो 7 ⊕ 3 ⊖ 2 क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"14"},"4":{"en":"19"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"⊕ → × and ⊖ → −<br>7 ⊕ 3 = 7 × 3 = 21<br>21 ⊖ 2 = 21 − 2 = 19<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 19.</b>","hi":"⊕ → × तथा ⊖ → −<br>7 ⊕ 3 = 7 × 3 = 21<br>21 ⊖ 2 = 21 − 2 = 19<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 19 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074689","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"As per the Venn diagram given in the image, what is the number of backward uneducated women who are employed?<br>Note: In the Venn diagram, the big circle represents “Employed women”, the small circle represents “Backward women”, and the triangle represents “Educated women”.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197ca04-6ca9-7ee1-918a-5ef7dbcd490b_EN.jpg?edu=639294378590956647\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"छवि में दिए गए वेन आरेख के अनुसार, पिछड़ी अशिक्षित महिलाओं की संख्या कितनी है जो नियोजित हैं?<br>नोट: वेन आरेख में बड़ा वृत्त “नियोजित महिलाएँ”, छोटा वृत्त “पिछड़ी महिलाएँ” तथा त्रिभुज “शिक्षित महिलाएँ” को दर्शाता है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197ca04-6ca9-7ee1-918a-5ef7dbcd490b_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725619116\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"34"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"14"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Big circle = employed women, small circle = backward women, triangle = educated women.<br>Backward and uneducated means the small circle but not the triangle; backward women who are also employed means the region common to the small circle and the big circle.<br>This region (small circle ∩ big circle, outside the triangle) contains the number 10.<br>The number 6 is the region common to all three (backward, educated and employed), 22 belongs to backward + educated, 34 to backward only, so none of these is the required region.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10.</b>","hi":"बड़ा वृत्त = नियोजित महिलाएँ, छोटा वृत्त = पिछड़ी महिलाएँ, त्रिभुज = शिक्षित महिलाएँ।<br>पिछड़ी तथा अशिक्षित का अर्थ है छोटे वृत्त का वह भाग जो त्रिभुज में नहीं है; और पिछड़ी महिलाएँ जो नियोजित भी हैं, अर्थात् छोटे वृत्त और बड़े वृत्त का उभयनिष्ठ भाग।<br>इस भाग (छोटा वृत्त ∩ बड़ा वृत्त, त्रिभुज के बाहर) में संख्या 10 है।<br>संख्या 6 तीनों का उभयनिष्ठ भाग है (पिछड़ी, शिक्षित तथा नियोजित), 22 पिछड़ी + शिक्षित है, 34 केवल पिछड़ी है, अतः ये अभीष्ट भाग नहीं हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197ca04-6ca9-7ee1-918a-5ef7dbcd490b_EN.jpg?edu=639294378590956647","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197ca04-6ca9-7ee1-918a-5ef7dbcd490b_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725619116"]}},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074690","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Pick the correct figure from Image Y to continue the series established in Image X.<br>Image X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197ceee-11f4-735a-9b2e-775b8fe4a69c_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591107706\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"छवि X में स्थापित श्रृंखला को आगे बढ़ाने के लिए छवि Y में से सही आकृति चुनिए।<br>छवि X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197ceee-11f4-735a-9b2e-775b8fe4a69c_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725736957\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In Image X the small arrow attached to the square keeps changing its position in the same order around the square — first it points downwards, then towards the right, then towards the upper right and then towards the upper left.<br>Continuing this movement, in the next figure the arrow must lie on the left side of the square and point towards the left.<br>This is exactly figure (D) of Image Y.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): D.</b>","hi":"छवि X में वर्ग से जुड़ा छोटा तीर वर्ग के चारों ओर एक ही क्रम में अपनी स्थिति बदलता रहता है — पहले नीचे, फिर दाईं ओर, फिर ऊपर-दाईं ओर तथा फिर ऊपर-बाईं ओर।<br>इसी क्रम को आगे बढ़ाने पर अगली आकृति में तीर वर्ग के बाईं ओर होकर बाईं ओर संकेत करेगा।<br>छवि Y में यही आकृति (D) है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): D है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197ceee-11f4-735a-9b2e-775b8fe4a69c_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591107706","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197ceee-11f4-735a-9b2e-775b8fe4a69c_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725736957"]}},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074691","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"From Image Y, pick the box that looks like the one created by folding the paper sheet in Image X.<br>Image X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197d03c-ad1a-728d-ae55-5228c8726c35_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591268550\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"छवि Y में से वह बक्सा चुनिए जो छवि X में दी गई कागज़ की शीट को मोड़कर बनाए गए बक्से जैसा दिखता है।<br>छवि X:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197d03c-ad1a-728d-ae55-5228c8726c35_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725860612\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the net there are three star faces, one circle face, one square face and one blank (shaded) face.<br>On folding the net, the circle and the square come on opposite faces of the cube, so they can never be seen together — options (B) and (C) are ruled out.<br>The first and the third star of the upper row are separated by the circle, so they also become opposite faces; hence all three stars can never be seen at the same time — option (D), which shows a star on all the three visible faces, is ruled out.<br>Option (A) shows a star, the circle and the blank face; the circle is adjacent to every face of the four-face ring around it, so a star and the blank face can both appear next to the circle.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A.</b>","hi":"दिए गए जाल (net) में तीन तारा फलक, एक वृत्त फलक, एक वर्ग फलक और एक खाली (छायांकित) फलक है।<br>जाल को मोड़ने पर वृत्त और वर्ग घन के विपरीत फलकों पर आते हैं, इसलिए ये कभी एक साथ नहीं दिख सकते — विकल्प (B) और (C) असंभव हैं।<br>ऊपरी पंक्ति के पहले और तीसरे तारे के बीच वृत्त है, अतः ये दोनों भी विपरीत फलक बनते हैं; इसलिए तीनों तारे एक साथ कभी नहीं दिख सकते — विकल्प (D), जिसमें तीनों दृश्य फलकों पर तारा है, असंभव है।<br>विकल्प (A) में तारा, वृत्त तथा खाली फलक दिखते हैं; वृत्त अपने चारों आस-पास के फलकों से सटा है, अतः तारा और खाली फलक दोनों वृत्त के साथ दिख सकते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): A है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/0197d03c-ad1a-728d-ae55-5228c8726c35_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591268550","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/0197d03c-ad1a-728d-ae55-5228c8726c35_HI.jpg?edu=639294378725860612"]}},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074692","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Select the Venn diagram that best illustrates the relationship between the following classes.<br>Army, Indian Constitution, Indian President [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह वेन आरेख चुनिए जो निम्नलिखित वर्गों के बीच संबंध को सर्वोत्तम रूप से दर्शाता है।<br>सेना, भारतीय संविधान, भारत के राष्ट्रपति [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d66b16f330_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591481214\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd99cf024505_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726025617\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d7d4c8ce85_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591514355\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd9a687b41b0_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726050226\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d897f2a35b_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591548149\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd9bc632578b_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726078164\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d948846037_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591585277\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd9cedbc16f1_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726102855\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The Army works under the rules laid down by the Indian Constitution, and the Indian President is the Supreme Commander of the Army and also functions within the constitutional set-up.<br>Hence all the three classes are related to one another in a graded manner, which is shown by three concentric circles (one inside the other).<br>The second figure shows only partial overlapping, the third shows three intersecting circles and the fourth shows two intersecting circles inside a larger circle, so none of them fits.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1).</b>","hi":"सेना भारतीय संविधान द्वारा निर्धारित नियमों के अंतर्गत कार्य करती है, और भारत के राष्ट्रपति सेना के सर्वोच्च कमांडर होने के साथ-साथ संवैधानिक व्यवस्था के अंतर्गत ही कार्य करते हैं।<br>अतः तीनों वर्ग एक-दूसरे से क्रमिक रूप से संबंधित हैं, जिसे तीन संकेंद्रित वृत्तों (एक-दूसरे के भीतर) द्वारा दर्शाया जाता है।<br>दूसरी आकृति में केवल आंशिक अतिव्याप्ति, तीसरी में तीन प्रतिच्छेदी वृत्त तथा चौथी में बड़े वृत्त के भीतर दो प्रतिच्छेदी वृत्त हैं, इसलिए कोई भी उपयुक्त नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d66b16f330_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591481214","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd99cf024505_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726025617"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d7d4c8ce85_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591514355","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd9a687b41b0_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726050226"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d897f2a35b_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591548149","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd9bc632578b_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726078164"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019836f0-66bb-79a1-92a6-b3d948846037_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591585277","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983b90-3930-7104-936a-fd9cedbc16f1_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726102855"]}}},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074693","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Two different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the number that will be on the face opposite to the one having ‘6’.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/01983ff2-cb7f-767b-a711-67dea5d080fe_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591636445\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ही पासे की दो भिन्न स्थितियाँ दर्शाई गई हैं। उस संख्या का चयन करें जो ‘6’ वाले फलक के विपरीत फलक पर होगी।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983ff2-cb7f-767b-a711-67dea5d080fe_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726142293\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the first position, 6 is adjacent to 3 and 1.<br>In the second position, 2 is also adjacent to 1 and 3.<br>So the numbers 6 and 2 have exactly the same two neighbouring faces; two faces having the same set of adjacent faces must lie opposite each other.<br>Therefore 2 is opposite to 6.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2.</b>","hi":"पहली स्थिति में 6, संख्याओं 3 और 1 के साथ सटा है।<br>दूसरी स्थिति में 2 भी 1 और 3 के साथ सटा है।<br>अर्थात् 6 और 2 के आस-पास के फलक ठीक समान हैं; जिन दो फलकों के साथी फलक समान हों, वे एक-दूसरे के विपरीत होते हैं।<br>इसलिए 2, संख्या 6 के विपरीत है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/01983ff2-cb7f-767b-a711-67dea5d080fe_EN.jpg?edu=639294378591636445","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/01983ff2-cb7f-767b-a711-67dea5d080fe_HI.jpg?edu=639294378726142293"]}},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074694","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The rule for a specific set of centre IDs is: The sum of the digits must be a multiple of 7. Which centre ID is valid? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक विशिष्ट समूह के सेंटर ID का नियम है: अंकों का योग 7 का गुणज होना चाहिए। कौन-सा सेंटर ID मान्य है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4823"},"2":{"en":"9113"},"3":{"en":"5542"},"4":{"en":"6398"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Sum of the digits of each option:<br>4823 → 4 + 8 + 2 + 3 = 17 (not a multiple of 7)<br>9113 → 9 + 1 + 1 + 3 = 14 (14 = 2 × 7 ✓)<br>5542 → 5 + 5 + 4 + 2 = 16 (not a multiple of 7)<br>6398 → 6 + 3 + 9 + 8 = 26 (not a multiple of 7)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 9113.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक विकल्प के अंकों का योग:<br>4823 → 4 + 8 + 2 + 3 = 17 (7 का गुणज नहीं)<br>9113 → 9 + 1 + 1 + 3 = 14 (14 = 2 × 7 ✓)<br>5542 → 5 + 5 + 4 + 2 = 16 (7 का गुणज नहीं)<br>6398 → 6 + 3 + 9 + 8 = 26 (7 का गुणज नहीं)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 9113 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074695","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a cross-cultural pitch, an international stakeholder smiles warmly and nods continuously. However, the next day, they firmly reject your business proposal via email. How should you process this conflicting outcome? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बहु-सांस्कृतिक प्रस्तुति के दौरान एक अंतरराष्ट्रीय हितधारक गर्मजोशी से मुस्कुराते हैं और लगातार सिर हिलाते हैं। लेकिन अगले दिन वे ई-मेल के माध्यम से आपके व्यावसायिक प्रस्ताव को दृढ़ता से अस्वीकार कर देते हैं। इस परस्पर विरोधी परिणाम को आप कैसे समझेंगे? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Confront the stakeholder directly regarding their highly deceptive and manipulative behaviour.","hi":"हितधारक के अत्यधिक भ्रामक और चालाकीपूर्ण व्यवहार के बारे में उनसे सीधे टकराव करें।"},"2":{"en":"Assume the pitch was fundamentally flawed and rewrite the entire business plan immediately.","hi":"मान लें कि प्रस्तुति मूल रूप से त्रुटिपूर्ण थी और तुरंत पूरी व्यावसायिक योजना फिर से लिखें।"},"3":{"en":"Realise the nodding indicated polite attention rather than agreement and adjust future readings.","hi":"यह समझें कि सिर हिलाना सहमति के बजाय विनम्र ध्यान का संकेत था और आगे ऐसे संकेतों की व्याख्या में सुधार करें।"},"4":{"en":"Refuse to engage with the stakeholder further to avoid any future cross-cultural confusion.","hi":"भविष्य में किसी भी बहु-सांस्कृतिक भ्रम से बचने के लिए हितधारक से आगे बातचीत करने से इनकार कर दें।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In many cultures continuous smiling and nodding only show polite attention and do not mean agreement, so the rejection is not deceptive behaviour.<br>The right response is to understand this cultural difference and to read such signals correctly in future meetings, instead of blaming the stakeholder, rewriting the whole plan or refusing to deal with them.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Realise the nodding indicated polite attention rather than agreement and adjust future readings.</b>","hi":"अनेक संस्कृतियों में लगातार मुस्कुराना और सिर हिलाना केवल विनम्र ध्यान दर्शाता है, सहमति नहीं; इसलिए प्रस्ताव अस्वीकार करना भ्रामक व्यवहार नहीं है।<br>उचित प्रतिक्रिया यही है कि इस सांस्कृतिक अंतर को समझें तथा आगे की बैठकों में ऐसे संकेतों को सही ढंग से पढ़ें, न कि हितधारक पर दोष लगाएँ, पूरी योजना दोबारा लिखें या उनसे बातचीत बंद कर दें।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): यह समझें कि सिर हिलाना सहमति के बजाय विनम्र ध्यान का संकेत था और आगे ऐसे संकेतों की व्याख्या में सुधार करें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074696","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are travelling on a crowded bus. An elderly passenger enters, and though several people notice, everyone remains seated. To ensure immediate civic consideration for the passenger while avoiding public conflict or unnecessary attention, what is the best action to take? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप एक भीड़भाड़ वाली बस में यात्रा कर रहे हैं। एक वृद्ध यात्री प्रवेश करते हैं और कई लोग देखने के बावजूद सभी बैठे रहते हैं। यात्री के प्रति तत्काल नागरिक शिष्टाचार सुनिश्चित करने तथा सार्वजनिक टकराव या अनावश्यक ध्यान से बचने के लिए सर्वोत्तम कार्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignore the situation and stay seated, assuming that another passenger will eventually offer their seat.","hi":"स्थिति को नज़रअंदाज़ करते हुए बैठे रहें और यह मान लें कि कोई अन्य यात्री अंततः अपनी सीट दे देगा।"},"2":{"en":"Stand up to offer your own seat immediately, doing so politely and without drawing public attention to the action.","hi":"तुरंत अपनी सीट देने के लिए खड़े हो जाएँ, तथा यह कार्य विनम्रता से बिना सार्वजनिक ध्यान आकर्षित किए करें।"},"3":{"en":"Remain seated but speak up loudly to criticize the surrounding passengers for not giving up their seats.","hi":"बैठे रहें परंतु आस-पास के यात्रियों की सीट न देने के लिए ज़ोर से आवाज़ उठाकर आलोचना करें।"},"4":{"en":"Take out your mobile phone to record video of the seated passengers to publicly shame them on social media.","hi":"बैठे हुए यात्रियों का वीडियो बनाने के लिए मोबाइल निकालें ताकि उन्हें सोशल मीडिया पर सार्वजनिक रूप से शर्मिंदा किया जा सके।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Civic responsibility demands that help is given at once, without waiting for others.<br>Offering your own seat politely and quietly solves the problem immediately and also avoids any argument or unwanted attention.<br>Criticising others loudly or shaming them on social media creates conflict and does not help the elderly passenger.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Stand up to offer your own seat immediately, doing so politely and without drawing public attention to the action.</b>","hi":"नागरिक जिम्मेदारी यह कहती है कि दूसरों की प्रतीक्षा किए बिना तुरंत सहायता दी जाए।<br>अपनी सीट विनम्रता से और बिना शोर-शराबे के दे देना समस्या का तुरंत समाधान करता है और किसी बहस या अनचाहे ध्यान से भी बचाता है।<br>दूसरों की ज़ोर से आलोचना करना या सोशल मीडिया पर अपमानित करना टकराव पैदा करता है और वृद्ध यात्री की कोई सहायता नहीं करता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): तुरंत अपनी सीट देने के लिए खड़े हो जाएँ, तथा यह कार्य विनम्रता से बिना सार्वजनिक ध्यान आकर्षित किए करें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074697","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A recent study indicates that individuals who eat breakfast regularly are less likely to develop obesity and other health issues.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Skipping breakfast leads to obesity and other health issues.<br>II. Eating breakfast regularly can prevent obesity and other health problems.<br>III. People who are obese should avoid eating breakfast. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, चाहे वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>हाल के एक अध्ययन से संकेत मिलता है कि जो व्यक्ति नियमित रूप से नाश्ता करते हैं, उनमें मोटापा और अन्य स्वास्थ्य समस्याएँ होने की संभावना कम होती है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. नाश्ता छोड़ने से मोटापा और अन्य स्वास्थ्य समस्याएँ होती हैं।<br>II. नियमित रूप से नाश्ता करना मोटापा और अन्य स्वास्थ्य समस्याओं को रोक सकता है।<br>III. मोटापे से ग्रस्त व्यक्तियों को नाश्ता करने से बचना चाहिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"4":{"en":"Only Inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The statement only says that people who eat breakfast regularly are less likely to become obese, i.e. eating breakfast regularly protects against obesity and related problems — this is exactly Inference II.<br>Inference I is too strong: the statement nowhere says that skipping breakfast causes obesity.<br>Inference III is not supported at all; the statement advises eating breakfast, not avoiding it.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Inference II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल इतना कहता है कि जो लोग नियमित रूप से नाश्ता करते हैं, उनमें मोटापा होने की संभावना कम होती है, अर्थात् नियमित नाश्ता मोटापा और संबंधित समस्याओं से बचाव कर सकता है — यही अनुमान II है।<br>अनुमान I अत्यधिक है: कथन में कहीं भी यह नहीं कहा गया कि नाश्ता छोड़ने से मोटापा होता है।<br>अनुमान III कथन से समर्थित नहीं है; कथन नाश्ता करने की बात करता है, उससे बचने की नहीं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074698","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>After introducing an online appointment system, the hospital reported a significant reduction in patient waiting time.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The online appointment system may have contributed to the reduction in waiting time.<br>II. The online appointment system may have completely eliminated waiting time for all patients. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते है/हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>ऑनलाइन अपॉइंटमेंट प्रणाली शुरू करने के बाद अस्पताल ने रोगियों के प्रतीक्षा समय में उल्लेखनीय कमी दर्ज की।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. ऑनलाइन अपॉइंटमेंट प्रणाली ने प्रतीक्षा समय में कमी में योगदान दिया हो सकता है।<br>II. ऑनलाइन अपॉइंटमेंट प्रणाली ने सभी रोगियों के प्रतीक्षा समय को पूरी तरह समाप्त कर दिया हो सकता है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The statement speaks of a ‘significant reduction’ in waiting time after the new system was introduced, so it is quite possible that the system contributed to that reduction — conclusion I follows.<br>Conclusion II talks of complete elimination of waiting time for all patients, which is far beyond the statement, where only a reduction is reported — conclusion II does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"कथन में नई प्रणाली लागू होने के बाद प्रतीक्षा समय में ‘उल्लेखनीय कमी’ की बात कही गई है, अतः यह संभव है कि प्रणाली ने उस कमी में योगदान दिया हो — निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।<br>निष्कर्ष II में सभी रोगियों के प्रतीक्षा समय के पूर्णतः समाप्त होने की बात है, जो कथन से बहुत आगे है, क्योंकि कथन में केवल कमी बताई गई है — निष्कर्ष II नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074699","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The central bank has raised the repo rate by 50 basis points to curb the inflationary pressure being experienced by the economy.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. An increase in the repo rate is an effective instrument for managing inflation.<br>II. The central bank has complete control over all external factors contributing to inflation. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अधोलिखित पूर्वधारणाओं को ध्यान से पढ़िए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी पूर्वधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>केंद्रीय बैंक ने अर्थव्यवस्था में अनुभव की जा रही मुद्रास्फीतिक दबाव को नियंत्रित करने के लिए रेपो दर में 50 आधार अंकों की वृद्धि की है।<br><b>पूर्वधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. रेपो दर में वृद्धि मुद्रास्फीति के प्रबंधन का एक प्रभावी साधन है।<br>II. केंद्रीय बैंक का मुद्रास्फीति में योगदान देने वाले सभी बाह्य कारकों पर पूर्ण नियंत्रण है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल पूर्वधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"पूर्वधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल पूर्वधारणा II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो पूर्वधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The bank is raising the repo rate ‘to curb inflationary pressure’, which means it assumes that a higher repo rate actually helps in controlling inflation — Assumption I is implicit.<br>Nothing in the statement suggests that the bank controls all external factors of inflation, and no organisation can assume such complete control — Assumption II is not implicit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"बैंक ‘मुद्रास्फीतिक दबाव को नियंत्रित करने के लिए’ रेपो दर बढ़ा रहा है, अर्थात् बैंक यह मानकर चल रहा है कि अधिक रेपो दर मुद्रास्फीति नियंत्रित करने में सहायक होती है — पूर्वधारणा I निहित है।<br>कथन में कहीं से यह नहीं निकलता कि बैंक का मुद्रास्फीति के सभी बाह्य कारकों पर नियंत्रण है, और कोई संस्था ऐसा पूर्ण नियंत्रण मान नहीं सकती — पूर्वधारणा II निहित नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल पूर्वधारणा I निहित है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074700","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Four different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the number that will be on the face opposite to the one showing ‘2’.<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019edaa5-889b-7cb1-8430-fba3b0b7658a_EN.jpg?edu=639294378593406360\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ही पासे की चार भिन्न स्थितियाँ दर्शाई गई हैं। उस संख्या का चयन करें जो ‘2’ दर्शाने वाले फलक के विपरीत फलक पर होगी।<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019edaa5-889b-7cb1-8430-fba3b0b7658a_HI.jpg?edu=639294378727483273\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the first position, 2 is adjacent to 6 and 5.<br>In the fourth position, 3 is adjacent to the same two numbers 6 and 5.<br>Only two faces can be adjacent to the pair 6 – 5, and those two faces are opposite to each other.<br>Therefore 2 and 3 lie on opposite faces, i.e. 3 is opposite to 2.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3.</b>","hi":"पहली स्थिति में 2, संख्याओं 6 और 5 के साथ सटा है।<br>चौथी स्थिति में 3 भी उन्हीं दो संख्याओं 6 और 5 के साथ सटा है।<br>युग्म 6 – 5 के साथ केवल दो ही फलक सटे हो सकते हैं और वे दोनों एक-दूसरे के विपरीत होते हैं।<br>इसलिए 2 और 3 विपरीत फलकों पर हैं, अर्थात् 2 के विपरीत 3 है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019edaa5-889b-7cb1-8430-fba3b0b7658a_EN.jpg?edu=639294378593406360","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019edaa5-889b-7cb1-8430-fba3b0b7658a_HI.jpg?edu=639294378727483273"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074701","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019edb8b-02d5-7f15-9105-4e408e5349ca_EN.jpg?edu=639294378593715994\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) और (e) से चिह्नित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति शेष चार के समान नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो बाकियों से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019edb8b-02d5-7f15-9105-4e408e5349ca_HI.jpg?edu=639294378727714425\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"b"},"2":{"en":"e"},"3":{"en":"d"},"4":{"en":"a"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In figures (a), (b), (c) and (d) one shaded triangle is the image of the other shaded triangle obtained by turning the figure about the centre of the square — that is, the two black portions are placed symmetrically about the centre.<br>In figure (e) this symmetry is absent: the two black triangles are not the turned (or mirror) image of each other about the centre of the square, so this figure is different.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): e.</b>","hi":"आकृति (a), (b), (c) और (d) में एक छायांकित त्रिभुज दूसरे छायांकित त्रिभुज का वर्ग के केंद्र के परितः घुमाने पर प्राप्त प्रतिबिंब है — अर्थात् दोनों काला भाग केंद्र के परितः सममित हैं।<br>आकृति (e) में यह सममिति नहीं है: दोनों काले त्रिभुज वर्ग के केंद्र के परितः एक-दूसरे के घुमाया गया (या दर्पण) प्रतिबिंब नहीं हैं, इसलिए यह आकृति भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): e है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019edb8b-02d5-7f15-9105-4e408e5349ca_EN.jpg?edu=639294378593715994","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019edb8b-02d5-7f15-9105-4e408e5349ca_HI.jpg?edu=639294378727714425"]}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074702","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019edbc1-624e-787e-b81d-a385e3682f56_EN.jpg?edu=639294378594041741\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) और (e) से चिह्नित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार समान हैं। परंतु एक आकृति शेष चार के समान नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो बाकियों से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019edbc1-624e-787e-b81d-a385e3682f56_HI.jpg?edu=639294378727971468\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"e"},"2":{"en":"c"},"3":{"en":"d"},"4":{"en":"a"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each hexagon is divided into six triangles. In figures (a), (b), (d) and (e) the two shaded triangles are placed away from each other — they are separated by at least one unshaded triangle.<br>In figure (c) the two shaded triangles are adjacent to each other and lie on the same side of the hexagon, so this figure is different from the rest.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): c.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक षट्भुज छह त्रिभुजों में विभाजित है। आकृति (a), (b), (d) और (e) में दोनों छायांकित त्रिभुज एक-दूसरे से दूर हैं — उनके बीच कम से कम एक अछायांकित त्रिभुज है।<br>आकृति (c) में दोनों छायांकित त्रिभुज एक-दूसरे से सटे हुए हैं तथा षट्भुज के एक ही ओर हैं, इसलिए यह आकृति बाकियों से भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): c है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019edbc1-624e-787e-b81d-a385e3682f56_EN.jpg?edu=639294378594041741","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019edbc1-624e-787e-b81d-a385e3682f56_HI.jpg?edu=639294378727971468"]}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074703","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks (_) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific pattern in the given order.<br><b>r _ sr _ tsrrt _ rr _ sr</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"रिक्त स्थानों (_) को निम्नलिखित चार विकल्पों में से एक से भरें ताकि श्रृंखला दिए गए क्रम में एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न का पालन करे।<br><b>r _ sr _ tsrrt _ rr _ sr</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ttss"},"2":{"en":"tsts"},"3":{"en":"trst"},"4":{"en":"sstt"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Put option (3), trst:<br>r <b>t</b> sr <b>r</b> tsrrt <b>s</b> rr <b>t</b> sr<br>On writing the letters continuously we get:<br>r t s r | r t s r | r t s r | r t s r<br>The group ‘rtsr’ repeats four times, so the series follows a definite pattern with option (3).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): trst.</b>","hi":"विकल्प (3), trst रखने पर:<br>r <b>t</b> sr <b>r</b> tsrrt <b>s</b> rr <b>t</b> sr<br>अक्षरों को क्रम से लिखने पर प्राप्त होता है:<br>r t s r | r t s r | r t s r | r t s r<br>समूह ‘rtsr’ चार बार दोहराता है, अतः विकल्प (3) से श्रृंखला एक निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): trst है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074704","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"<b>Policy:</b> A firm approves work-from-home (WFH) if the employee’s ratings are ≥ 4.0/5.0 for each of the last two quarters and the role is remote-eligible. However, a manager will override and deny WFH if there is an ongoing disciplinary inquiry, even when both approval criteria are met.<br><b>Employee Profile:</b><br>• Ratings: 4.2/5.0 in the previous quarter and 4.5/5.0 in the current quarter<br>• Role: Remote-eligible<br>• Disciplinary Status: No ongoing inquiry<br><b>Question:</b> Based on the firm’s policy, what is the correct action to take regarding this employee’s WFH request? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>नीति:</b> एक कंपनी कर्मचारी को वर्क-फ्रॉम-होम (WFH) की स्वीकृति तब देती है जब कर्मचारी की रेटिंग पिछली दोनों तिमाहियों में ≥ 4.0/5.0 हो तथा पद रिमोट-योग्य हो। किंतु यदि किसी चल रही अनुशासनात्मक जाँच हो तो प्रबंधक स्वीकृति के दोनों मानदंड पूरे होने पर भी WFH अस्वीकार कर सकता है।<br><b>कर्मचारी का विवरण:</b><br>• रेटिंग: पिछली तिमाही में 4.2/5.0 तथा वर्तमान तिमाही में 4.5/5.0<br>• पद: रिमोट-योग्य<br>• अनुशासनात्मक स्थिति: कोई चल रही जाँच नहीं<br><b>प्रश्न:</b> कंपनी की नीति के आधार पर इस कर्मचारी के WFH अनुरोध पर सही कार्रवाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Approve WFH","hi":"WFH स्वीकृत करें"},"2":{"en":"Deny WFH","hi":"WFH अस्वीकार करें"},"3":{"en":"Refer the case to HR","hi":"मामला मानव संसाधन विभाग को भेजें"},"4":{"en":"Approve WFH for one quarter only","hi":"केवल एक तिमाही के लिए WFH स्वीकृत करें"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Both approval criteria are satisfied:<br>• Ratings — 4.2 and 4.5, both ≥ 4.0 ✓<br>• Role — remote-eligible ✓<br>• Disciplinary status — no ongoing inquiry, so there is no ground for the manager to override the approval.<br>Therefore the request must simply be approved.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Approve WFH.</b>","hi":"स्वीकृति के दोनों मानदंड पूरे होते हैं:<br>• रेटिंग — 4.2 तथा 4.5, दोनों ≥ 4.0 ✓<br>• पद — रिमोट-योग्य ✓<br>• अनुशासनात्मक स्थिति — कोई चल रही जाँच नहीं, अतः प्रबंधक के पास अस्वीकृति का कोई आधार नहीं है।<br>इसलिए अनुरोध सीधे स्वीकृत किया जाना चाहिए।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): WFH स्वीकृत करें।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074705","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Find the odd one out. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विषम अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"BDFH"},"2":{"en":"JLNP"},"3":{"en":"TVXZ"},"4":{"en":"CEIK"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Position of the letters in the alphabet:<br>BDFH → 2, 4, 6, 8 (each letter is 2 more than the previous one)<br>JLNP → 10, 12, 14, 16 (difference of 2)<br>TVXZ → 20, 22, 24, 26 (difference of 2)<br>CEIK → 3, 5, 9, 11 (the difference 5 → 9 is 4, not 2)<br>In CEIK the letters do not move with a constant gap of 2, so it is the odd one out.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): CEIK.</b>","hi":"अक्षरों का वर्णमाला में स्थान:<br>BDFH → 2, 4, 6, 8 (प्रत्येक अक्षर पिछले से 2 अधिक)<br>JLNP → 10, 12, 14, 16 (अंतर 2)<br>TVXZ → 20, 22, 24, 26 (अंतर 2)<br>CEIK → 3, 5, 9, 11 (5 से 9 का अंतर 4 है, 2 नहीं)<br>CEIK में अक्षर लगातार 2 के अंतर से नहीं बढ़ते, इसलिए यह विषम है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): CEIK है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074706","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Give the name of the Indian Origin deceased NASA Astronaut on whose name On October 2, 2020, NASA had launched a commercial spacecraft. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"उस भारतीय मूल की दिवंगत NASA अंतरिक्ष यात्री का नाम बताइए, जिनके नाम पर 2 अक्टूबर 2020 को NASA ने एक वाणिज्यिक अंतरिक्ष यान प्रक्षेपित किया था। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Raja Jon Vurputur Chari","hi":"राजा जॉन वुरपुटूर चारी"},"2":{"en":"Sunita Chawla","hi":"सुनीता चावला"},"3":{"en":"Sunita Williams","hi":"सुनीता विलियम्स"},"4":{"en":"Kalpana Chawla","hi":"कल्पना चावला"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Kalpana Chawla</b><br>On <b>2 October 2020</b>, NASA launched the <b>Cygnus NG-14</b> commercial cargo spacecraft named <b>S.S. Kalpana Chawla</b>, after the Indian-origin astronaut who died in the <b>Columbia</b> disaster.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Kalpana Chawla</b> was born in <b>Karnal, Haryana</b>, and became the <b>first woman of Indian origin</b> to fly in space, on the <b>Space Shuttle Columbia in 1997</b>.<br>• She died on <b>1 February 2003</b> when the Space Shuttle <b>Columbia (STS-107)</b> broke up on re-entry.<br>• She was awarded the <b>Congressional Space Medal of Honor</b> posthumously and has a <b>NASA supercomputer and an asteroid</b> named after her.<br>• <b>Raja Chari</b> is a serving NASA astronaut of Indian origin, <b>Sunita Williams</b> is an Indian-origin astronaut, and Cygnus spacecraft are named after deceased astronauts.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – कल्पना चावला</b><br><b>2 अक्टूबर 2020</b> को NASA ने <b>सिग्नस NG-14</b> वाणिज्यिक मालवाहक अंतरिक्ष यान <b>एस.एस. कल्पना चावला</b> नाम से प्रक्षेपित किया, जो <b>कोलंबिया</b> हादसे में निधन हुई भारतीय मूल की अंतरिक्ष यात्री के नाम पर था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कल्पना चावला</b> का जन्म <b>करनाल, हरियाणा</b> में हुआ और वे <b>1997</b> में <b>स्पेस शटल कोलंबिया</b> से उड़ान भरने वाली <b>भारतीय मूल की पहली महिला</b> बनीं।<br>• <b>1 फरवरी 2003</b> को पुनः प्रवेश के समय स्पेस शटल <b>कोलंबिया (STS-107)</b> के टूट जाने से उनका निधन हुआ।<br>• उन्हें मरणोपरांत <b>कांग्रेसनल स्पेस मेडल ऑफ ऑनर</b> दिया गया तथा <b>NASA सुपरकंप्यूटर एवं एक क्षुद्रग्रह</b> का नाम उनके नाम पर रखा गया।<br>• <b>राजा चारी</b> भारतीय मूल के सेवारत NASA अंतरिक्ष यात्री हैं, <b>सुनीता विलियम्स</b> भारतीय मूल की अंतरिक्ष यात्री हैं, तथा सिग्नस यानों का नाम दिवंगत अंतरिक्ष यात्रियों पर रखा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074707","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements:<br>1. As per Article 343 of the Indian Constitution, the Hindi language, written in the Devanagari script, is recognised as the \"official language of the Central Government\".<br>2. The Constitution permits the continuation of English for official purposes indefinitely and does not mention any Commission or Committee on Official Language.<br>Which of the above statements is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार करें:<br>1. भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 343 के अनुसार देवनागरी लिपि में हिंदी भाषा को \"केंद्र सरकार की राजभाषा\" के रूप में मान्यता प्राप्त है।<br>2. संविधान राजभाषा प्रयोजनों के लिए अंग्रेजी के अनिश्चितकाल तक प्रयोग की अनुमति देता है तथा राजभाषा पर किसी आयोग अथवा समिति का उल्लेख नहीं करता।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 तथा 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न 1 और न 2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Only 1</b><br>Statement 1 is correct because <b>Article 343(1)</b> declares that the official language of the Union shall be <b>Hindi in Devanagari script</b>. Statement 2 is wrong because the Constitution provides for a <b>Commission on Official Language (Article 344)</b> and a <b>Committee on Official Language</b>, and English was continued only for a limited period, later extended by law.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 343(2)</b> allowed English to continue for <b>15 years</b> from the commencement of the Constitution, that is up to <b>1965</b>.<br>• The <b>Official Languages Act, 1963</b> provided for the continued use of English for official purposes of the Union, and the <b>Official Languages Rules, 1976</b> lay down the details.<br>• <b>Article 344</b> provides for a <b>Commission on Official Language</b> at the expiry of five years and of ten years, and a <b>Committee of Parliament on Official Language</b> to examine its recommendations.<br>• The <b>Eighth Schedule</b> now lists <b>22 languages</b>, and Hindi is the official language, not the national language, of India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1</b><br>कथन 1 सही है क्योंकि <b>अनुच्छेद 343(1)</b> घोषित करता है कि संघ की राजभाषा <b>देवनागरी लिपि में हिंदी</b> होगी। कथन 2 गलत है क्योंकि संविधान में <b>राजभाषा आयोग (अनुच्छेद 344)</b> तथा <b>राजभाषा समिति</b> का प्रावधान है और अंग्रेजी को केवल सीमित अवधि के लिए जारी रखा गया था, जिसे बाद में विधि द्वारा बढ़ाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 343(2)</b> ने संविधान के प्रारंभ से <b>15 वर्ष</b> अर्थात <b>1965</b> तक अंग्रेजी को जारी रखने की अनुमति दी।<br>• <b>राजभाषा अधिनियम, 1963</b> ने संघ के राजकीय प्रयोजनों के लिए अंग्रेजी के सतत प्रयोग का प्रावधान किया तथा <b>राजभाषा नियम, 1976</b> विवरण देते हैं।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 344</b> में पाँच वर्ष तथा दस वर्ष पूरे होने पर <b>राजभाषा आयोग</b> तथा उसकी सिफारिशों की जाँच हेतु <b>संसदीय राजभाषा समिति</b> का प्रावधान है।<br>• <b>आठवीं अनुसूची</b> में अब <b>22 भाषाएँ</b> हैं, तथा हिंदी भारत की राजभाषा है, राष्ट्रभाषा नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074708","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In Kho-Kho, what is the term for the player sitting in the square facing the direction of play? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"खो-खो में खेल की दिशा की ओर मुँह करके बैठे खिलाड़ी को क्या कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chaser","hi":"चेज़र"},"2":{"en":"Runner","hi":"रनर"},"3":{"en":"Attacker","hi":"आक्रामक"},"4":{"en":"Defender","hi":"रक्षक"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Chaser</b><br>In <b>Kho-Kho</b>, the team that sits in the squares is the <b>chasing team</b>, and its players are called <b>chasers</b>, while the defending team players are <b>runners</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The chaser who sits in the square with his back to the direction of play is called the <b>active chaser</b>, and he starts the game after the word \"kho\".<br>• The active chaser chases opponents and can give <b>kho</b> to a sitting teammate by tapping him on the back.<br>• Kho-Kho is played between two teams of <b>12 players each</b>, of which <b>9 take the field</b>, on a rectangular court with <b>two poles</b>.<br>• The <b>Kho-Kho Federation of India</b> governs the sport, and it was included in the <b>Asian Games</b> and the <b>Khelo India</b> programme.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – चेज़र</b><br><b>खो-खो</b> में जो टीम चौकों में बैठती है, वह <b>खदेड़ने वाली टीम</b> होती है और उसके खिलाड़ियों को <b>चेज़र</b> कहा जाता है, जबकि बचाव करने वाली टीम के खिलाड़ी <b>रनर</b> होते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• खेल की दिशा के विपरीत मुँह करके चौक में बैठे चेज़र को <b>सक्रिय चेज़र</b> कहा जाता है, जो \"खो\" शब्द के बाद खेल आरंभ करता है।<br>• सक्रिय चेज़र प्रतिद्वंद्वियों का पीछा करता है तथा साथी को पीठ पर थपकी देकर <b>खो</b> दे सकता है।<br>• खो-खो <b>12-12 खिलाड़ियों</b> की दो टीमों के बीच खेला जाता है, जिसमें <b>9 खिलाड़ी मैदान में</b> उतरते हैं; मैदान आयताकार तथा इसमें <b>दो खंभे</b> होते हैं।<br>• इस खेल का नियामक <b>भारतीय खो-खो महासंघ</b> है, तथा इसे <b>एशियाई खेलों</b> और <b>खेलो इंडिया</b> कार्यक्रम में शामिल किया गया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074709","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a benefit received by a retired President of India? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा लाभ भारत के सेवानिवृत्त राष्ट्रपति को प्राप्त होता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lifetime free international travel for self and spouse","hi":"स्वयं तथा जीवनसाथी के लिए आजीवन निःशुल्क अंतर्राष्ट्रीय यात्रा"},"2":{"en":"Appointment as Governor of a State with Cabinet rank benefits","hi":"मंत्रिमंडल स्तर के लाभों के साथ राज्य के राज्यपाल के रूप में नियुक्ति"},"3":{"en":"Rent-free furnished bungalow, personal staff, and 2.5 lakh monthly pension","hi":"किराया मुक्त सुसज्जित बंगला, व्यक्तिगत स्टाफ तथा 2.5 लाख रुपये मासिक पेंशन"},"4":{"en":"Membership to the Rajya Sabha for life","hi":"आजीवन राज्यसभा सदस्यता"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Rent-free furnished bungalow, personal staff, and 2.5 lakh monthly pension</b><br>A retired President of India is entitled to a <b>rent-free furnished bungalow</b> for life, <b>personal staff</b>, secretarial assistance, and a <b>monthly pension of 2.5 lakh rupees</b>, apart from other facilities.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• These benefits are provided under the <b>President's Emoluments and Pension Act, 1951</b> and related rules.<br>• A retired President is also entitled to <b>free medical treatment, travel facilities, and security cover</b> as per government rules.<br>• The <b>salary of the President</b> is charged on the <b>Consolidated Fund of India</b> and cannot be reduced during his term.<br>• Article <b>59</b> lays down the qualifications of the President, and <b>Article 61</b> provides the procedure for <b>impeachment</b> for violation of the Constitution.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – किराया मुक्त सुसज्जित बंगला, व्यक्तिगत स्टाफ तथा 2.5 लाख रुपये मासिक पेंशन</b><br>भारत के सेवानिवृत्त राष्ट्रपति को आजीवन <b>किराया मुक्त सुसज्जित बंगला</b>, <b>व्यक्तिगत स्टाफ</b>, सचिवालय सहायता तथा <b>2.5 लाख रुपये मासिक पेंशन</b> सहित अन्य सुविधाएँ प्राप्त होती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ये लाभ <b>राष्ट्रपति के वेतन तथा पेंशन अधिनियम, 1951</b> तथा संबंधित नियमों के अंतर्गत दिए जाते हैं।<br>• सेवानिवृत्त राष्ट्रपति को सरकारी नियमों के अनुसार <b>निःशुल्क चिकित्सा, यात्रा सुविधाएँ तथा सुरक्षा</b> भी मिलती हैं।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रपति का वेतन</b> <b>भारत के समेकित निधि</b> पर भारित होता है और कार्यकाल में इसे घटाया नहीं जा सकता।<br>• अनुच्छेद <b>59</b> राष्ट्रपति की योग्यताएँ निर्धारित करता है तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 61</b> संविधान के उल्लंघन पर <b>महाभियोग</b> की प्रक्रिया देता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074710","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Consider the following pairs of Indian musical instruments and their types:<br>1. Chinkara - Stringed instrument<br>2. Ghatam - Percussion instrument<br>3. Kartal - Percussion/clapper instrument<br>Which of the above pairs is/are <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय वाद्यों तथा उनके प्रकार के निम्नलिखित युग्मों पर विचार करें:<br>1. चिंकारा - तत वाद्य<br>2. घटम - अवनद्ध वाद्य<br>3. करताल - अवनद्ध/झंकार वाद्य<br>उपर्युक्त में से कौन-सा/से युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है/हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1 and 2","hi":"केवल 1 तथा 2"},"2":{"en":"Only 2 and 3","hi":"केवल 2 तथा 3"},"3":{"en":"Only 1 and 3","hi":"केवल 1 तथा 3"},"4":{"en":"All 1, 2 and 3","hi":"1, 2 तथा 3 सभी"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – All 1, 2 and 3</b><br>All three pairs are correct: the <b>chinkara</b> is a <b>stringed instrument</b>, the <b>ghatam</b> is a <b>percussion instrument</b> made of clay, and the <b>kartal</b> is a <b>clapper or percussion instrument</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>chinkara</b> is a folk stringed instrument of Rajasthan, played with a bow, and is associated with the <b>Langa and Manganiyar</b> communities.<br>• The <b>ghatam</b> is a clay pot used in <b>Carnatic music</b>, played with the fingers and palms, and is associated with artists such as <b>T.H. Vinayakram</b>.<br>• The <b>kartal</b> consists of wooden clappers used in <b>bhajan and folk music</b> of Rajasthan and Gujarat.<br>• Indian instruments are traditionally classified into <b>tat (stringed), sushir (wind), avanaddha (membrane) and ghan (solid)</b> types.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 1, 2 तथा 3 सभी</b><br>तीनों युग्म सही हैं: <b>चिंकारा</b> <b>तत वाद्य</b> है, <b>घटम</b> मिट्टी से बना <b>अवनद्ध वाद्य</b> है तथा <b>करताल</b> <b>झंकार अथवा ताल वाद्य</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>चिंकारा</b> राजस्थान का लोक तत वाद्य है, जिसे गज से बजाया जाता है और यह <b>लंगा तथा मांगणियार</b> समुदायों से जुड़ा है।<br>• <b>घटम</b> मिट्टी का घड़ा है जो <b>कर्नाटक संगीत</b> में प्रयुक्त होता है, इसे अंगुलियों तथा हथेलियों से बजाया जाता है; यह <b>टी.एच. विनायकराम</b> जैसे कलाकारों से जुड़ा है।<br>• <b>करताल</b> लकड़ी की खटकनों से बनता है और राजस्थान एवं गुजरात के <b>भजन तथा लोक संगीत</b> में प्रयुक्त होता है।<br>• भारतीय वाद्य परंपरागत रूप से <b>तत (तार), सुषिर (वायु), अवनद्ध (चर्म) तथा घन (ठोस)</b> में वर्गीकृत हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074711","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"The World Happiness Report combines well-being data from how many countries? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट कितने देशों के कल्याण संबंधी आँकड़ों को सम्मिलित करती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Over 70","hi":"70 से अधिक"},"2":{"en":"Over 100","hi":"100 से अधिक"},"3":{"en":"Over 140","hi":"140 से अधिक"},"4":{"en":"Over 200","hi":"200 से अधिक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Over 140</b><br>The <b>World Happiness Report</b> combines well-being data from <b>more than 140 countries</b>, ranking them on life evaluation and related factors.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The report is prepared by the <b>Wellbeing Research Centre at the University of Oxford</b> with <b>Gallup</b> and the <b>UN Sustainable Development Solutions Network</b>.<br>• Rankings are based on the <b>Cantril ladder</b>, in which respondents rate their current life on a scale of 0 to 10.<br>• The six explanatory factors are <b>GDP per capita, social support, healthy life expectancy, freedom to make life choices, generosity and perceptions of corruption</b>.<br>• It is released every year around <b>20 March</b>, the <b>International Day of Happiness</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 140 से अधिक</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट</b> <b>140 से अधिक देशों</b> के कल्याण संबंधी आँकड़ों को सम्मिलित करती है और उन्हें जीवन मूल्यांकन तथा संबंधित कारकों पर रैंक करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• रिपोर्ट <b>ऑक्सफोर्ड विश्वविद्यालय के वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर</b> द्वारा <b>गैलप</b> तथा <b>संयुक्त राष्ट्र सतत विकास समाधान नेटवर्क</b> के साथ तैयार होती है।<br>• रैंकिंग <b>कैंट्रिल लैडर</b> पर आधारित है, जिसमें उत्तरदाता अपने वर्तमान जीवन को 0 से 10 के पैमाने पर आँकते हैं।<br>• छह व्याख्यात्मक कारक हैं <b>प्रति व्यक्ति जीडीपी, सामाजिक सहायता, स्वस्थ जीवन प्रत्याशा, जीवन चुनने की स्वतंत्रता, उदारता तथा भ्रष्टाचार की धारणा</b>।<br>• यह प्रतिवर्ष <b>20 मार्च</b> को <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय प्रसन्नता दिवस</b> के आसपास जारी होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074712","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In weightlifting, what does the term \"snatch\" refer to? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारोत्तोलन में \"स्नैच\" शब्द किसे दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lifting barbell from floor to overhead in one continuous motion","hi":"बारबेल को फर्श से सिर के ऊपर एक सतत गति में उठाना"},"2":{"en":"Lifting the barbell to the shoulders before pressing overhead","hi":"सिर के ऊपर दबाने से पहले बारबेल को कंधों तक उठाना"},"3":{"en":"A warm-up exercise before competition","hi":"प्रतियोगिता से पहले का वार्म-अप व्यायाम"},"4":{"en":"A penalty given for incorrect lifting technique","hi":"गलत उठाने की तकनीक पर दिया जाने वाला दंड"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Lifting barbell from floor to overhead in one continuous motion</b><br>The <b>snatch</b> is one of the two lifts in Olympic weightlifting, in which the barbell is lifted from the floor to <b>overhead in a single continuous movement</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The other Olympic lift is the <b>clean and jerk</b>, which has two phases - lifting to the shoulders and then jerking overhead.<br>• A lifter gets <b>three attempts</b> in each lift, and the best successful attempt in each counts towards the total.<br>• Competitors are ranked by the <b>total of the best snatch and best clean and jerk</b>, and ties are broken by <b>body weight</b>.<br>• <b>Mirabai Chanu</b> won the silver medal for India in the <b>49 kg category</b> at the Tokyo Olympics 2020.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बारबेल को फर्श से सिर के ऊपर एक सतत गति में उठाना</b><br><b>स्नैच</b> ओलंपिक भारोत्तोलन के दो उठानों में से एक है, जिसमें बारबेल को <b>एक ही सतत गति</b> में फर्श से <b>सिर के ऊपर</b> उठाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दूसरा ओलंपिक उठान <b>क्लीन एंड जर्क</b> है, जिसके दो चरण होते हैं - कंधों तक उठाना और फिर सिर के ऊपर झटका देना।<br>• भारोत्तोलक को प्रत्येक उठान में <b>तीन प्रयास</b> मिलते हैं और प्रत्येक के सर्वश्रेष्ठ सफल प्रयास का योग लिया जाता है।<br>• प्रतिभागियों की रैंकिंग <b>सर्वश्रेष्ठ स्नैच तथा सर्वश्रेष्ठ क्लीन एंड जर्क के कुल</b> से होती है और बराबरी पर <b>शरीर भार</b> से निर्णय होता है।<br>• <b>मीराबाई चानू</b> ने टोक्यो ओलंपिक 2020 में <b>49 किलो वर्ग</b> में भारत के लिए रजत पदक जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074713","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: South Indian History & Tripartite Struggle and Cholas","question":{"en":"What is the <b>correct</b> description of the Vesara style of temple architecture? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मंदिर स्थापत्य की वेसर शैली का <b>सही</b> वर्णन क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A fusion of Nagara and Dravidian styles, mainly in Deccan.","hi":"नागर तथा द्रविड़ शैलियों का मिश्रण, मुख्यतः दक्कन में।"},"2":{"en":"A Mughal adaptation of Persian domes","hi":"फारसी गुंबदों का मुगल अनुकूलन"},"3":{"en":"A Buddhist style using chaityas and vihara","hi":"चैत्य तथा विहार का प्रयोग करने वाली बौद्ध शैली"},"4":{"en":"A colonial revival seen in European churches","hi":"यूरोपीय गिरजाघरों में दिखने वाला औपनिवेशिक पुनरुद्धार"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – A fusion of Nagara and Dravidian styles, mainly in Deccan.</b><br>The <b>Vesara style</b> is a <b>hybrid of the Nagara and Dravidian styles</b> that developed mainly in the <b>Deccan</b> region under the <b>Chalukyas, Hoysalas and Rashtrakutas</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Features include a <b>stepped pyramidal vimana</b>, ornate <b>pillars and lathe-turned columns</b>, and a curved shikhara with Dravidian elements.<br>• Famous examples are the <b>Chennakesava temple at Belur, Hoysaleswara at Halebidu, and the temples of Badami and Aihole</b>.<br>• The <b>Nagara style</b> is characterised by a <b>curvilinear shikhara</b> and is found in north India, while the <b>Dravidian style</b> has a <b>pyramidal vimana and gopurams</b> in the south.<br>• The <b>Kailasa temple at Ellora</b>, built by the Rashtrakutas, is a famous rock-cut example of Deccan temple architecture.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नागर तथा द्रविड़ शैलियों का मिश्रण, मुख्यतः दक्कन में।</b><br><b>वेसर शैली</b> <b>नागर तथा द्रविड़ शैलियों का मिश्रित रूप</b> है, जो मुख्यतः <b>दक्कन</b> क्षेत्र में <b>चालुक्य, होयसल तथा राष्ट्रकूट</b> शासकों के अधीन विकसित हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसकी विशेषताओं में <b>सोपानाकार पिरामिडी विमान</b>, अलंकृत <b>स्तंभ तथा खरादे पर बने स्तंभ</b>, और द्रविड़ तत्वों के साथ वक्र शिखर शामिल हैं।<br>• प्रसिद्ध उदाहरण <b>बेलूर का चेन्नाकेसव मंदिर, हलेबिडु का होयसलेश्वर मंदिर तथा बादामी एवं ऐहोले के मंदिर</b> हैं।<br>• <b>नागर शैली</b> की विशेषता <b>वक्र रेखीय शिखर</b> है और यह उत्तर भारत में मिलती है, जबकि <b>द्रविड़ शैली</b> में <b>पिरामिडी विमान तथा गोपुरम</b> दक्षिण में होते हैं।<br>• राष्ट्रकूटों द्वारा निर्मित <b>एलोरा का कैलास मंदिर</b> दक्कन स्थापत्य का प्रसिद्ध शैलकृत उदाहरण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074714","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was appointed as the Chief Election Commissioner of India in May 2022? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मई 2022 में भारत के मुख्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया था? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajiv Kumar","hi":"राजीव कुमार"},"2":{"en":"Sushil Chandra","hi":"सुशील चंद्र"},"3":{"en":"Nasim Zaidi","hi":"नसीम जैदी"},"4":{"en":"Achal Kumar Jyoti","hi":"अचल कुमार ज्योति"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Rajiv Kumar</b><br><b>Rajiv Kumar</b> took charge as the <b>Chief Election Commissioner of India</b> in <b>May 2022</b>, succeeding <b>Sushil Chandra</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He is a former <b>IAS officer of the Jharkhand cadre</b> and earlier served as <b>Election Commissioner</b> and as <b>Finance Secretary</b>.<br>• The <b>Election Commission</b> is a constitutional body under <b>Article 324</b>, consisting of the <b>Chief Election Commissioner and two Election Commissioners</b>.<br>• The CEC can be removed only in the manner of a <b>Supreme Court judge</b>, while other Election Commissioners are removed on the recommendation of the CEC.<br>• Under the <b>CEC and Other Election Commissioners Act, 2023</b>, appointments are made by the President on the recommendation of a committee of the <b>Prime Minister, a Union Minister and the Leader of the Opposition</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – राजीव कुमार</b><br><b>राजीव कुमार</b> ने <b>मई 2022</b> में <b>सुशील चंद्र</b> के स्थान पर <b>भारत के मुख्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त</b> का पदभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे <b>झारखंड कैडर</b> के पूर्व <b>आईएएस अधिकारी</b> हैं और इससे पहले <b>निर्वाचन आयुक्त</b> तथा <b>वित्त सचिव</b> रहे।<br>• <b>निर्वाचन आयोग</b> <b>अनुच्छेद 324</b> के अंतर्गत संवैधानिक निकाय है, जिसमें <b>मुख्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त तथा दो निर्वाचन आयुक्त</b> होते हैं।<br>• CEC को केवल <b>सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश</b> की रीति से हटाया जा सकता है, जबकि अन्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त CEC की सिफारिश पर हटाए जाते हैं।<br>• <b>CEC तथा अन्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त अधिनियम, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत नियुक्तियाँ <b>प्रधानमंत्री, एक केंद्रीय मंत्री तथा लोकसभा में विपक्ष के नेता</b> की समिति की सिफारिश पर राष्ट्रपति करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074715","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which Indian state's Khecheopalri Lake was declared a Ramsar site in February 2025? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस भारतीय राज्य की खेचेओपलरी झील को फरवरी 2025 में रामसर स्थल घोषित किया गया? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sikkim","hi":"सिक्किम"},"2":{"en":"Himachal Pradesh","hi":"हिमाचल प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Uttarakhand","hi":"उत्तराखंड"},"4":{"en":"Arunachal Pradesh","hi":"अरुणाचल प्रदेश"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Sikkim</b><br><b>Khecheopalri Lake</b> in <b>West Sikkim</b> was declared a <b>Ramsar site in February 2025</b>, making it one of India's wetland sites of international importance.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The lake is a <b>sacred wetland</b> for both Buddhists and Hindus and is associated with the legend that birds do not allow a leaf to float on its waters.<br>• It lies near <b>Pelling</b> and forms part of the <b>Khangchendzonga Biosphere Reserve</b> landscape.<br>• The <b>Ramsar Convention</b> on wetlands was signed in <b>1971 in Ramsar, Iran</b>, and India joined it in <b>1982</b>.<br>• India now has more than <b>90 Ramsar sites</b>, the highest number in Asia, with <b>Chilika</b> and <b>Keoladeo</b> among the earliest.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सिक्किम</b><br><b>पश्चिम सिक्किम</b> की <b>खेचेओपलरी झील</b> को <b>फरवरी 2025</b> में <b>रामसर स्थल</b> घोषित किया गया, जिससे यह अंतर्राष्ट्रीय महत्व की भारत की आर्द्रभूमियों में शामिल हो गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह झील बौद्ध तथा हिंदू दोनों के लिए <b>पवित्र आर्द्रभूमि</b> है और इससे जुड़ी मान्यता है कि पक्षी इसके जल पर पत्ता तैरने नहीं देते।<br>• यह <b>पेलिंग</b> के निकट स्थित है और <b>कंचनजंगा जीवमंडल रिजर्व</b> परिदृश्य का भाग है।<br>• आर्द्रभूमि पर <b>रामसर अभिसमय</b> <b>1971</b> में <b>ईरान के रामसर</b> में हस्ताक्षरित हुआ तथा भारत <b>1982</b> में इसका सदस्य बना।<br>• भारत में अब <b>90 से अधिक रामसर स्थल</b> हैं, जो एशिया में सर्वाधिक हैं; <b>चिल्का</b> तथा <b>केवलादेव</b> इनमें सर्वप्रमुख हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074716","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"The term \"cognizable offence\" refers to an offence where: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\"संज्ञेय अपराध\" शब्द उस अपराध को दर्शाता है जहाँ: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An FIR cannot be registered","hi":"प्रथम सूचना रिपोर्ट दर्ज नहीं की जा सकती"},"2":{"en":"The Magistrate has to permit arrest","hi":"मजिस्ट्रेट को गिरफ्तारी की अनुमति देनी होती है"},"3":{"en":"The police officer can arrest without warrant","hi":"पुलिस अधिकारी बिना वारंट गिरफ्तार कर सकता है"},"4":{"en":"A person can only be summoned","hi":"व्यक्ति को केवल समन किया जा सकता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The police officer can arrest without warrant</b><br>A <b>cognizable offence</b> is one in which a police officer may <b>arrest without a warrant</b> and may start investigation without the order of a Magistrate.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Section <b>2(1)(g)</b> of the <b>BNSS, 2023</b> defines a cognizable offence, and <b>Section 2(1)(l)</b> defines a non-cognizable offence.<br>• In a <b>non-cognizable offence</b>, the police cannot arrest without a warrant and need the Magistrate's order to investigate.<br>• An <b>FIR</b> is registered for a cognizable offence under <b>Section 173</b> of the BNSS, while information about a non-cognizable offence is entered in the <b>General Diary</b>.<br>• The BNSS replaced the <b>Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पुलिस अधिकारी बिना वारंट गिरफ्तार कर सकता है</b><br><b>संज्ञेय अपराध</b> वह है जिसमें पुलिस अधिकारी <b>बिना वारंट गिरफ्तार</b> कर सकता है तथा मजिस्ट्रेट के आदेश के बिना जाँच आरंभ कर सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>BNSS, 2023</b> की धारा <b>2(1)(ग)</b> संज्ञेय अपराध को परिभाषित करती है तथा धारा <b>2(1)(ल)</b> असंज्ञेय अपराध को।<br>• <b>असंज्ञेय अपराध</b> में पुलिस बिना वारंट गिरफ्तार नहीं कर सकती और जाँच के लिए मजिस्ट्रेट का आदेश आवश्यक होता है।<br>• संज्ञेय अपराध में BNSS की धारा <b>173</b> के अंतर्गत <b>प्रथम सूचना रिपोर्ट</b> दर्ज होती है, जबकि असंज्ञेय अपराध की सूचना <b>सामान्य डायरी</b> में दर्ज की जाती है।<br>• BNSS ने <b>दंड प्रक्रिया संहिता, 1973</b> का स्थान लिया और यह <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074717","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"What innovative technologies will the TDS01 mission test? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"TDS01 मिशन किन नवीन तकनीकों का परीक्षण करेगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Quantum communication and electric propulsion","hi":"क्वांटम संचार तथा विद्युत प्रणोदन"},"2":{"en":"Artificial intelligence in space navigation","hi":"अंतरिक्ष नौवहन में कृत्रिम बुद्धिमत्ता"},"3":{"en":"Advanced space telescopes","hi":"उन्नत अंतरिक्ष दूरबीनें"},"4":{"en":"Robotic space mining techniques","hi":"रोबोटिक अंतरिक्ष खनन तकनीकें"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Quantum communication and electric propulsion</b><br>The <b>TDS-01</b> mission of ISRO is designed to test <b>quantum communication technologies</b> along with <b>electric propulsion</b> systems in orbit.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Quantum communication</b> uses the principles of quantum mechanics, such as <b>entanglement and the no-cloning theorem</b>, to make data transfer secure.<br>• <b>Electric propulsion</b> uses electrical energy to ionise a propellant and accelerate it, giving very high <b>specific impulse</b> and saving propellant mass.<br>• ISRO has already demonstrated <b>electric propulsion</b> on the <b>GSAT-9 and GSAT-20</b> class satellites for station-keeping.<br>• TDS-01 is an experimental satellite intended to build capability for <b>secure satellite-based communication</b> and future space missions.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – क्वांटम संचार तथा विद्युत प्रणोदन</b><br>इसरो का <b>TDS-01</b> मिशन कक्षा में <b>क्वांटम संचार तकनीक</b> तथा <b>विद्युत प्रणोदन</b> प्रणालियों का परीक्षण करने हेतु तैयार किया गया है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>क्वांटम संचार</b> क्वांटम यांत्रिकी के सिद्धांतों, जैसे <b>उलझाव तथा अनुकरण-निषेध प्रमेय</b>, का उपयोग कर डेटा स्थानांतरण को सुरक्षित बनाता है।<br>• <b>विद्युत प्रणोदन</b> में विद्युत ऊर्जा से प्रणोदक को आयनित कर त्वरित किया जाता है, जिससे अत्यधिक <b>विशिष्ट आवेग</b> मिलता है और प्रणोदक भार बचता है।<br>• इसरो ने <b>जीसैट-9 तथा जीसैट-20</b> श्रेणी के उपग्रहों में स्टेशन-कीपिंग हेतु <b>विद्युत प्रणोदन</b> पहले ही प्रदर्शित किया है।<br>• TDS-01 एक प्रायोगिक उपग्रह है, जिसका उद्देश्य <b>सुरक्षित उपग्रह आधारित संचार</b> तथा भविष्य के अंतरिक्ष मिशनों की क्षमता विकसित करना है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074718","section":"GK","topic":"Chemistry: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which gas is known as \"laughing gas\"? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सी गैस \"हँसने वाली गैस\" के रूप में जानी जाती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nitrous oxide (N2O)","hi":"नाइट्रस ऑक्साइड (N2O)"},"2":{"en":"Nitric oxide (NO)","hi":"नाइट्रिक ऑक्साइड (NO)"},"3":{"en":"Carbon dioxide (CO2)","hi":"कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड (CO2)"},"4":{"en":"Sulfur dioxide (SO2)","hi":"सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड (SO2)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Nitrous oxide (N2O)</b><br><b>Nitrous oxide (N2O)</b> is called <b>laughing gas</b> because inhaling it produces a feeling of euphoria and mild hysteria; it is used as an <b>anaesthetic</b> in dentistry and surgery.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• N2O is prepared by heating <b>ammonium nitrate</b> and is a colourless gas with a slightly sweet smell.<br>• It is also a <b>potent greenhouse gas</b>, about <b>270 times</b> more effective than carbon dioxide over a 100-year period.<br>• <b>Nitric oxide (NO)</b> is a signalling molecule in the body, and <b>nitrogen dioxide (NO2)</b> is a brown toxic gas that causes acid rain.<br>• <b>Carbon dioxide</b> is used in fire extinguishers and photosynthesis, while <b>sulphur dioxide</b> causes acid rain and respiratory problems.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नाइट्रस ऑक्साइड (N2O)</b><br><b>नाइट्रस ऑक्साइड (N2O)</b> को <b>हँसने वाली गैस</b> कहा जाता है क्योंकि इसके सेवन से प्रसन्नता तथा हल्की उन्माद जैसी अनुभूति होती है; यह दंत चिकित्सा तथा शल्य चिकित्सा में <b>निश्चेतक</b> के रूप में प्रयुक्त होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• N2O <b>अमोनियम नाइट्रेट</b> को गर्म करके बनाई जाती है और यह हल्की मीठी गंध वाली रंगहीन गैस है।<br>• यह एक <b>शक्तिशाली ग्रीनहाउस गैस</b> भी है, जो 100 वर्षों में कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड से लगभग <b>270 गुना</b> अधिक प्रभावी है।<br>• <b>नाइट्रिक ऑक्साइड (NO)</b> शरीर में संकेत अणु है तथा <b>नाइट्रोजन डाइऑक्साइड (NO2)</b> भूरी विषैली गैस है जो अम्लीय वर्षा करती है।<br>• <b>कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड</b> अग्निशामक यंत्रों तथा प्रकाश संश्लेषण में प्रयुक्त होती है, जबकि <b>सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड</b> अम्लीय वर्षा तथा श्वसन संबंधी समस्याओं का कारण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074719","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Rocks, Continents, and Oceans","question":{"en":"The continent is mostly in the Southern Hemisphere and surrounded by two oceans; the Pacific Ocean on the west and the Atlantic Ocean on the east and north, the continent is: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यह महाद्वीप मुख्यतः दक्षिणी गोलार्ध में है और दो महासागरों से घिरा है; पश्चिम में प्रशांत महासागर तथा पूर्व और उत्तर में अटलांटिक महासागर, यह महाद्वीप है: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"South America","hi":"दक्षिण अमेरिका"},"2":{"en":"Africa","hi":"अफ्रीका"},"3":{"en":"Europe","hi":"यूरोप"},"4":{"en":"North America","hi":"उत्तरी अमेरिका"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – South America</b><br><b>South America</b> lies mostly in the <b>Southern Hemisphere</b>, with the <b>Pacific Ocean</b> to its west and the <b>Atlantic Ocean</b> to its east and north.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• South America is the <b>fourth largest continent</b> and is drained by the <b>Amazon</b>, the world's largest river by volume.<br>• It is home to the <b>Andes</b>, the longest continental mountain range, and the <b>Atacama Desert</b>, one of the driest places on earth.<br>• The continent has <b>12 countries</b> and two territories, with <b>Brazil</b> the largest and <b>Suriname</b> the smallest.<br>• The <b>Drake Passage</b> separates South America from Antarctica, and the <b>Panama Canal</b> links the Atlantic and Pacific oceans.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – दक्षिण अमेरिका</b><br><b>दक्षिण अमेरिका</b> मुख्यतः <b>दक्षिणी गोलार्ध</b> में स्थित है, जिसके पश्चिम में <b>प्रशांत महासागर</b> तथा पूर्व एवं उत्तर में <b>अटलांटिक महासागर</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दक्षिण अमेरिका <b>चौथा सबसे बड़ा महाद्वीप</b> है और यहाँ विश्व की जल-आयतन में सबसे बड़ी नदी <b>अमेज़न</b> बहती है।<br>• यहाँ <b>एंडीज़</b> स्थित है, जो सबसे लंबी महाद्वीपीय पर्वत श्रृंखला है, तथा <b>अटाकामा मरुस्थल</b>, जो विश्व के सर्वाधिक शुष्क क्षेत्रों में है।<br>• महाद्वीप में <b>12 देश</b> तथा दो क्षेत्र हैं, जिनमें <b>ब्राजील</b> सबसे बड़ा तथा <b>सूरीनाम</b> सबसे छोटा है।<br>• <b>ड्रेक जलडमरूमध्य</b> दक्षिण अमेरिका को अंटार्कटिका से अलग करता है तथा <b>पनामा नहर</b> अटलांटिक और प्रशांत महासागरों को जोड़ती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074720","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"Which Amendment transferred education from the State List to the Concurrent List? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस संशोधन ने शिक्षा को राज्य सूची से समवर्ती सूची में स्थानांतरित किया? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42nd Amendment","hi":"42वाँ संशोधन"},"2":{"en":"44th Amendment","hi":"44वाँ संशोधन"},"3":{"en":"73rd Amendment","hi":"73वाँ संशोधन"},"4":{"en":"86th Amendment","hi":"86वाँ संशोधन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 42nd Amendment</b><br>The <b>42nd Amendment Act, 1976</b> transferred <b>education, forests, weights and measures, protection of wild animals and birds, and administration of justice</b> from the State List to the <b>Concurrent List</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 42nd Amendment is called the <b>\"Mini Constitution\"</b> because of the large number of changes it made, including the addition of <b>Socialist, Secular and Integrity</b> to the Preamble.<br>• It added <b>Fundamental Duties (Article 51A)</b>, Part IVA, and provisions on <b>administrative tribunals</b>.<br>• The <b>44th Amendment, 1978</b> reversed several provisions of the 42nd Amendment and changed the ground of internal disturbance to <b>armed rebellion</b> for a national emergency.<br>• The <b>73rd Amendment</b> gave constitutional status to <b>Panchayati Raj</b> and the <b>86th Amendment</b> made education a fundamental right under <b>Article 21A</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 42वाँ संशोधन</b><br><b>42वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1976</b> ने <b>शिक्षा, वन, भार तथा माप, वन्य पशु-पक्षियों का संरक्षण तथा न्याय प्रशासन</b> को राज्य सूची से <b>समवर्ती सूची</b> में स्थानांतरित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 42वें संशोधन को इसके अनेक परिवर्तनों के कारण <b>\"लघु संविधान\"</b> कहा जाता है, जिसमें प्रस्तावना में <b>समाजवादी, धर्मनिरपेक्ष तथा अखंडता</b> जोड़ना शामिल है।<br>• इसने <b>मूल कर्तव्य (अनुच्छेद 51A)</b>, भाग IVA तथा <b>प्रशासनिक अधिकरणों</b> के प्रावधान जोड़े।<br>• <b>44वें संशोधन, 1978</b> ने 42वें संशोधन के कई प्रावधानों को बदला तथा राष्ट्रीय आपातकाल के आधार को आंतरिक गड़बड़ी से <b>सशस्त्र विद्रोह</b> में बदला।<br>• <b>73वें संशोधन</b> ने <b>पंचायती राज</b> को संवैधानिक दर्जा दिया तथा <b>86वें संशोधन</b> ने शिक्षा को <b>अनुच्छेद 21A</b> के अंतर्गत मूल अधिकार बनाया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074721","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Which scheme aims to improve groundwater management through community participation? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सी योजना सामुदायिक भागीदारी के माध्यम से भूजल प्रबंधन सुधारने का लक्ष्य रखती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National Aquifer Mapping Programme","hi":"राष्ट्रीय जलभृत मानचित्रण कार्यक्रम"},"2":{"en":"Jal Jeevan Mission","hi":"जल जीवन मिशन"},"3":{"en":"Atal Bhujal Yojana","hi":"अटल भूजल योजना"},"4":{"en":"Jal Kranti Abhiyan","hi":"जल क्रांति अभियान"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Atal Bhujal Yojana</b><br><b>Atal Bhujal Yojana</b> aims to improve <b>groundwater management</b> through <b>community participation</b>, especially in water-stressed areas.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The scheme was launched in <b>2020</b> with support from the <b>World Bank</b> and is implemented by the <b>Ministry of Jal Shakti</b>.<br>• It is being implemented in <b>seven states</b> - <b>Gujarat, Haryana, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Rajasthan and Uttar Pradesh</b> - in areas with depleted aquifers.<br>• It works through <b>Water User Associations and Panchayats</b>, promoting <b>demand-side management, crop diversification and recharge structures</b>.<br>• <b>Jal Jeevan Mission</b> focuses on <b>piped drinking water</b> to rural households, while the <b>National Aquifer Mapping Programme</b> maps aquifer geometry and quality.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अटल भूजल योजना</b><br><b>अटल भूजल योजना</b> का उद्देश्य <b>सामुदायिक भागीदारी</b> के माध्यम से <b>भूजल प्रबंधन</b> सुधारना है, विशेषकर जल-तनावग्रस्त क्षेत्रों में।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना <b>2020</b> में <b>विश्व बैंक</b> के सहयोग से आरंभ हुई और <b>जल शक्ति मंत्रालय</b> द्वारा क्रियान्वित की जाती है।<br>• यह <b>सात राज्यों</b> - <b>गुजरात, हरियाणा, कर्नाटक, मध्य प्रदेश, महाराष्ट्र, राजस्थान तथा उत्तर प्रदेश</b> - के रिक्त जलभृत वाले क्षेत्रों में लागू है।<br>• यह <b>जल उपयोगकर्ता संघों तथा पंचायतों</b> के माध्यम से कार्य करती है और <b>माँग पक्ष प्रबंधन, फसल विविधीकरण तथा पुनर्भरण संरचनाओं</b> को बढ़ावा देती है।<br>• <b>जल जीवन मिशन</b> ग्रामीण घरों को <b>नल से पेयजल</b> पर केंद्रित है, जबकि <b>राष्ट्रीय जलभृत मानचित्रण कार्यक्रम</b> जलभृतों की संरचना तथा गुणवत्ता का मानचित्रण करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074722","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the goal of India's Millet Mission (2023-25) in the context of economic geography? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आर्थिक भूगोल के संदर्भ में भारत के मिलेट मिशन (2023-25) का लक्ष्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increase foreign direct investment in agri-tech","hi":"कृषि तकनीक में प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश बढ़ाना"},"2":{"en":"Boost high-value urban rooftop farming","hi":"उच्च मूल्य वाली शहरी छत कृषि को बढ़ावा देना"},"3":{"en":"Promote climate-resilient farming in tribal/eastern regions","hi":"जनजातीय/पूर्वी क्षेत्रों में जलवायु-अनुकूल कृषि को बढ़ावा देना"},"4":{"en":"Export high-protein wheat to Africa","hi":"अफ्रीका को उच्च प्रोटीन गेहूँ का निर्यात करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Promote climate-resilient farming in tribal/eastern regions</b><br>India's <b>Millet Mission (2023-25)</b>, as part of the <b>Shree Anna</b> initiative, aims to promote <b>climate-resilient millet farming</b>, especially in <b>tribal and eastern regions</b> where these crops suit rainfed conditions.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India is the <b>largest producer of millets</b> in the world, and the <b>UN declared 2023 as the International Year of Millets</b> on India's proposal.<br>• Millets such as <b>ragi, jowar, bajra, kodo, kutki and little millet</b> need less water, tolerate poor soils and are nutritious.<br>• The mission supports <b>farmer producer organisations, processing units, value addition and marketing</b> of millets.<br>• Promoting millets helps <b>diversify cropping patterns</b> away from water-intensive paddy and wheat in the eastern and tribal belts.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जनजातीय/पूर्वी क्षेत्रों में जलवायु-अनुकूल कृषि को बढ़ावा देना</b><br>भारत का <b>मिलेट मिशन (2023-25)</b>, जो <b>श्री अन्न</b> पहल का भाग है, <b>जलवायु-अनुकूल मोटे अनाज की खेती</b> को बढ़ावा देता है, विशेषकर <b>जनजातीय तथा पूर्वी क्षेत्रों</b> में जहाँ ये फसलें वर्षा आधारित परिस्थितियों के अनुकूल हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत विश्व में <b>मोटे अनाज का सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक</b> है तथा भारत के प्रस्ताव पर <b>संयुक्त राष्ट्र ने 2023 को अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मिलेट वर्ष</b> घोषित किया।<br>• <b>रागी, ज्वार, बाजरा, कोदो, कुटकी तथा सामा</b> जैसे मोटे अनाज कम जल चाहते हैं, खराब मृदा सहते हैं और पोषक हैं।<br>• मिशन <b>किसान उत्पादक संगठनों, प्रसंस्करण इकाइयों, मूल्य संवर्धन तथा विपणन</b> को सहायता देता है।<br>• मोटे अनाज को बढ़ावा देने से पूर्वी तथा जनजातीय क्षेत्रों में <b>फसल प्रणाली का विविधीकरण</b> होकर अधिक जल माँगने वाले धान एवं गेहूँ पर निर्भरता घटती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074723","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"Which region is projected to face greatest aging stress in terms of care and dependency by 2036? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"2036 तक देखभाल तथा निर्भरता के संदर्भ में किस क्षेत्र में वृद्धावस्था का सर्वाधिक दबाव होने का अनुमान है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Central India (Chhattisgarh, MP)","hi":"मध्य भारत (छत्तीसगढ़, मध्य प्रदेश)"},"2":{"en":"North-East India","hi":"पूर्वोत्तर भारत"},"3":{"en":"Southern India (Kerala, Tamil Nadu)","hi":"दक्षिण भारत (केरल, तमिलनाडु)"},"4":{"en":"Jammu & Kashmir","hi":"जम्मू एवं कश्मीर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Southern India (Kerala, Tamil Nadu)</b><br>By <b>2036</b>, <b>southern India</b>, especially <b>Kerala and Tamil Nadu</b>, is projected to face the greatest <b>aging stress</b> in terms of care and dependency, because of low fertility and rising life expectancy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Kerala</b> has the highest proportion of elderly population among Indian states and one of the lowest total fertility rates.<br>• The <b>old-age dependency ratio</b> measures the number of persons aged 60 and above per 100 persons in the working age group.<br>• Rising aging stress increases demand for <b>healthcare, pensions and long-term care</b>, and reduces the working-age share of the population.<br>• India is undergoing a <b>demographic transition</b>, with some states ageing much faster than others, creating a <b>demographic divide</b> within the country.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – दक्षिण भारत (केरल, तमिलनाडु)</b><br><b>2036</b> तक <b>दक्षिण भारत</b>, विशेषकर <b>केरल तथा तमिलनाडु</b>, कम प्रजनन दर तथा बढ़ती जीवन प्रत्याशा के कारण देखभाल एवं निर्भरता की दृष्टि से सर्वाधिक <b>वृद्धावस्था दबाव</b> का सामना करेगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारतीय राज्यों में <b>केरल</b> में वृद्ध जनसंख्या का अनुपात सर्वाधिक है तथा कुल प्रजनन दर सबसे कम में से एक है।<br>• <b>वृद्धाश्रिता अनुपात</b> कार्यशील आयु वर्ग के प्रति 100 व्यक्तियों पर 60 वर्ष तथा अधिक आयु के व्यक्तियों की संख्या दर्शाता है।<br>• बढ़ता वृद्धावस्था दबाव <b>स्वास्थ्य सेवा, पेंशन तथा दीर्घकालिक देखभाल</b> की माँग बढ़ाता है और कार्यशील जनसंख्या का हिस्सा घटाता है।<br>• भारत <b>जनसांख्यिकीय संक्रमण</b> से गुजर रहा है, जिसमें कुछ राज्य दूसरों की तुलना में बहुत तेजी से वृद्ध हो रहे हैं, जिससे देश के भीतर <b>जनसांख्यिकीय विभाजन</b> उत्पन्न हो रहा है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074724","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: National News","question":{"en":"What was the estimated number of people displaced due to the 2024 monsoon floods in India? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत में 2024 के मानसूनी बाढ़ के कारण विस्थापित लोगों की अनुमानित संख्या कितनी थी? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.1 million","hi":"2.1 मिलियन"},"2":{"en":"3.7 million","hi":"3.7 मिलियन"},"3":{"en":"5.4 million","hi":"5.4 मिलियन"},"4":{"en":"7.8 million","hi":"7.8 मिलियन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 5.4 million</b><br>An estimated <b>5.4 million people</b> were displaced due to the <b>2024 monsoon floods</b> in India, according to assessments of the season's impact.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 2024 monsoon caused severe floods in <b>Assam, Tripura, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana, Kerala and parts of the northeast</b>.<br>• Displacement figures are compiled by agencies such as the <b>Internal Displacement Monitoring Centre</b> and the <b>NDMA</b> along with state governments.<br>• India is among the countries most exposed to <b>climate-related displacement</b>, due to floods, cyclones and drought.<br>• The <b>National Disaster Management Authority</b> coordinates relief, and the <b>National Disaster Response Force</b> carries out rescue operations.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 5.4 मिलियन</b><br>आकलन के अनुसार भारत में <b>2024 के मानसूनी बाढ़</b> के कारण अनुमानित <b>5.4 मिलियन लोग</b> विस्थापित हुए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2024 के मानसून ने <b>असम, त्रिपुरा, आंध्र प्रदेश, तेलंगाना, केरल तथा पूर्वोत्तर के कुछ भागों</b> में भीषण बाढ़ लाई।<br>• विस्थापन के आँकड़े <b>आंतरिक विस्थापन निगरानी केंद्र</b> तथा <b>NDMA</b> जैसी संस्थाओं द्वारा राज्य सरकारों के सहयोग से संकलित किए जाते हैं।<br>• बाढ़, चक्रवात तथा सूखे के कारण भारत <b>जलवायु संबंधी विस्थापन</b> के प्रति सर्वाधिक उजागर देशों में है।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रीय आपदा प्रबंधन प्राधिकरण</b> राहत का समन्वय करता है तथा <b>राष्ट्रीय आपदा प्रतिक्रिया बल</b> बचाव कार्य करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074725","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"The \"Strengthening the Quad Act\" passed by the U.S. House in 2024 primarily aimed at: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"2024 में अमेरिकी प्रतिनिधि सभा द्वारा पारित \"स्ट्रेंदनिंग द क्वाड अधिनियम\" का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Establishing a NATO-like military pact","hi":"नाटो जैसा सैन्य समझौता स्थापित करना"},"2":{"en":"Banning trade with non-Quad nations","hi":"गैर-क्वाड देशों के साथ व्यापार पर प्रतिबंध लगाना"},"3":{"en":"Formalizing coordination in innovation and security","hi":"नवाचार तथा सुरक्षा में समन्वय को औपचारिक रूप देना"},"4":{"en":"Dissolving AUKUS in favor of Quad","hi":"क्वाड के पक्ष में AUKUS को भंग करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Formalizing coordination in innovation and security</b><br>The <b>Strengthening the Quad Act</b>, passed by the <b>U.S. House of Representatives in 2024</b>, aimed at <b>formalising coordination</b> among the Quad countries in <b>innovation, technology and security</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Quad</b> is a grouping of <b>India, the United States, Japan and Australia</b>, revived in <b>2017</b> and elevated to leaders' level summits from <b>2021</b>.<br>• Its agenda covers <b>a free and open Indo-Pacific, maritime security, vaccine diplomacy, critical and emerging technologies, and resilient supply chains</b>.<br>• The Quad is <b>not a military alliance</b> and has no mutual defence treaty like NATO.<br>• Other Indo-Pacific groupings include <b>AUKUS</b> (Australia, UK, US) and the <b>I2U2</b> group with India, Israel, the UAE and the US.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – नवाचार तथा सुरक्षा में समन्वय को औपचारिक रूप देना</b><br><b>2024</b> में <b>अमेरिकी प्रतिनिधि सभा</b> द्वारा पारित <b>स्ट्रेंदनिंग द क्वाड अधिनियम</b> का उद्देश्य क्वाड देशों के बीच <b>नवाचार, तकनीक तथा सुरक्षा</b> में <b>समन्वय को औपचारिक रूप</b> देना था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>क्वाड</b> <b>भारत, संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका, जापान तथा ऑस्ट्रेलिया</b> का समूह है, जिसे <b>2017</b> में पुनर्जीवित किया गया और <b>2021</b> से शिखर सम्मेलन स्तर पर लाया गया।<br>• इसके एजेंडे में <b>स्वतंत्र एवं खुला हिंद-प्रशांत, समुद्री सुरक्षा, टीका कूटनीति, महत्वपूर्ण एवं उभरती तकनीक तथा सुदृढ़ आपूर्ति श्रृंखलाएँ</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• क्वाड <b>सैन्य गठबंधन नहीं</b> है और इसके पास नाटो जैसी कोई पारस्परिक रक्षा संधि नहीं है।<br>• अन्य हिंद-प्रशांत समूहों में <b>AUKUS</b> (ऑस्ट्रेलिया, ब्रिटेन, अमेरिका) तथा भारत, इज़राइल, यूएई और अमेरिका का <b>I2U2</b> समूह शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074726","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following is <b>NOT</b> a Rajput architectural example? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा <b>राजपूत</b> स्थापत्य का उदाहरण <b>नहीं</b> है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Amber Fort","hi":"आमेर का किला"},"2":{"en":"Mehrangarh Fort","hi":"मेहरानगढ़ का किला"},"3":{"en":"Udaipur City Palace","hi":"उदयपुर सिटी पैलेस"},"4":{"en":"Fatehpur Sikri","hi":"फतेहपुर सीकरी"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Fatehpur Sikri</b><br><b>Fatehpur Sikri</b> was built by the <b>Mughal emperor Akbar</b> and is a <b>Mughal</b> architectural complex, not a Rajput one, so it is the exception.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Amber Fort</b> and <b>Mehrangarh Fort</b> are Rajput hill forts of <b>Jaipur and Jodhpur</b>, known for their massive walls, courtyards and <b>jharokhas</b>.<br>• <b>Udaipur City Palace</b> is a Rajput palace complex on the bank of Lake Pichola, showing Rajput and Mughal influences.<br>• <b>Fatehpur Sikri</b> near Agra includes the <b>Buland Darwaza, Jama Masjid, Panch Mahal and Jodha Bai's palace</b> and is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.<br>• Rajput architecture is marked by <b>forts, palaces, havelis, jharokhas, chhatris and ornamental jali work</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – फतेहपुर सीकरी</b><br><b>फतेहपुर सीकरी</b> <b>मुगल सम्राट अकबर</b> द्वारा बनवाया गया <b>मुगल</b> स्थापत्य परिसर है, राजपूत नहीं, अतः यह अपवाद है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>आमेर का किला</b> तथा <b>मेहरानगढ़ का किला</b> <b>जयपुर एवं जोधपुर</b> के राजपूत दुर्ग हैं, जो विशाल दीवारों, आँगनों तथा <b>झरोखों</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध हैं।<br>• <b>उदयपुर सिटी पैलेस</b> पिछोला झील के किनारे राजपूत महल परिसर है, जिसमें राजपूत तथा मुगल प्रभाव दिखते हैं।<br>• आगरा के निकट <b>फतेहपुर सीकरी</b> में <b>बुलंद दरवाजा, जामा मस्जिद, पंच महल तथा जोधा बाई का महल</b> हैं और यह यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल है।<br>• राजपूत स्थापत्य की विशेषताएँ <b>किले, महल, हवेलियाँ, झरोखे, छतरियाँ तथा अलंकृत जाली का कार्य</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074727","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"The Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) replaces which of the following? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय न्याय संहिता (BNS) निम्नलिखित में से किसका स्थान लेती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Code of Civil Procedure","hi":"सिविल प्रक्रिया संहिता"},"2":{"en":"Indian Penal Code","hi":"भारतीय दंड संहिता"},"3":{"en":"Criminal Procedure Code","hi":"आपराधिक प्रक्रिया संहिता"},"4":{"en":"Indian Evidence Act","hi":"भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Indian Penal Code</b><br>The <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b> replaced the <b>Indian Penal Code, 1860</b>, the main substantive criminal law of India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>BNSS, 2023</b> replaced the <b>Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973</b>, which dealt with procedure.<br>• The <b>Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023</b> replaced the <b>Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b>.<br>• All three new laws came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b> and aim to modernise criminal justice, with emphasis on <b>digital evidence, time-bound investigation and trial</b>.<br>• The <b>Code of Civil Procedure, 1908</b> continues to govern civil procedure and was not replaced.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारतीय दंड संहिता</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> ने भारत के मुख्य आपराधिक विधि <b>भारतीय दंड संहिता, 1860</b> का स्थान लिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>BNSS, 2023</b> ने <b>दंड प्रक्रिया संहिता, 1973</b> का स्थान लिया, जो प्रक्रिया से संबंधित थी।<br>• <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023</b> ने <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872</b> का स्थान लिया।<br>• तीनों नई विधियाँ <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुईं और इनका उद्देश्य <b>डिजिटल साक्ष्य, समयबद्ध जाँच तथा विचारण</b> पर बल देते हुए आपराधिक न्याय को आधुनिक बनाना है।<br>• <b>सिविल प्रक्रिया संहिता, 1908</b> अभी भी सिविल प्रक्रिया को नियंत्रित करती है और उसे प्रतिस्थापित नहीं किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074728","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Baul songs of Bengal are best described as: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बंगाल के बाउल गीतों का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Martial songs performed during festivals","hi":"उत्सवों में गाए जाने वाले युद्ध गीत"},"2":{"en":"Romantic ballads of rural Rajasthan","hi":"ग्रामीण राजस्थान की प्रेम गाथाएँ"},"3":{"en":"Mystical, spiritual songs by wandering minstrels","hi":"घुमंतू भाटों द्वारा गाए जाने वाले रहस्यमय, आध्यात्मिक गीत"},"4":{"en":"Narrative ballads using a bow-shaped instrument","hi":"धनुषाकार वाद्य के साथ गाई जाने वाली आख्यान गाथाएँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Mystical, spiritual songs by wandering minstrels</b><br><b>Baul</b> songs of <b>Bengal</b> are <b>mystical and spiritual songs</b> sung by <b>wandering minstrels</b>, blending elements of <b>Vaishnavism, Sufism and Sahajiya</b> thought.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Baul tradition</b> is recognised by UNESCO as a <b>Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity</b>.<br>• Bauls sing with the <b>ektara, dotara, khamak and duggi</b> and use simple lyrics about the <b>inner journey and the divine within</b>.<br>• Famous Baul singers include <b>Lalan Fakir</b>, whose songs are collected in the <b>Lalan Geetika</b>, and <b>Purna Das Baul</b>.<br>• The <b>Baul</b> and <b>Marfa</b> traditions are both included in UNESCO's intangible heritage list from Bangladesh and India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – घुमंतू भाटों द्वारा गाए जाने वाले रहस्यमय, आध्यात्मिक गीत</b><br><b>बंगाल</b> के <b>बाउल</b> गीत <b>घुमंतू भाटों</b> द्वारा गाए जाने वाले <b>रहस्यमय एवं आध्यात्मिक गीत</b> हैं, जिनमें <b>वैष्णव, सूफी तथा सहजिया</b> विचारों का समन्वय है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>बाउल परंपरा</b> को यूनेस्को ने <b>मानवता की मौखिक एवं अमूर्त विरासत की उत्कृष्ट कृति</b> के रूप में मान्यता दी है।<br>• बाउल <b>एकतारा, दोतारा, खमक तथा डुग्गी</b> के साथ गाते हैं और उनके सरल बोल <b>आंतरिक यात्रा तथा भीतर स्थित दिव्यता</b> से संबंधित होते हैं।<br>• प्रसिद्ध बाउल गायकों में <b>लालन फकीर</b>, जिनके गीत <b>लालन गीतिका</b> में संग्रहीत हैं, तथा <b>पूर्ण दास बाउल</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>बाउल</b> तथा <b>मारफा</b> परंपराएँ बांग्लादेश और भारत से यूनेस्को की अमूर्त विरासत सूची में शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074729","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a narrative musical tradition from Tamil Nadu using a bow-shaped instrument? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी तमिलनाडु की आख्यान संगीत परंपरा है जिसमें धनुषाकार वाद्य का प्रयोग होता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Yakshagana","hi":"यक्षगान"},"2":{"en":"Villupattu","hi":"विल्लुपाट्टु"},"3":{"en":"Oppana","hi":"ओप्पाना"},"4":{"en":"Jhumur","hi":"झूमर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Villupattu</b><br><b>Villupattu</b> is a <b>narrative musical tradition of Tamil Nadu</b> in which the <b>villu</b>, a large <b>bow-shaped instrument</b> with bells, is used to accompany storytelling.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Performers strike the bow string with sticks while narrating stories from the <b>Ramayana, Mahabharata and local legends</b>.<br>• <b>Yakshagana</b> is a theatrical dance-drama form of <b>Karnataka</b>, and <b>Oppana</b> is a bridal dance of <b>Kerala Muslims</b>.<br>• <b>Jhumur</b> is a folk dance and song tradition of <b>Bengal, Jharkhand and Assam</b>, performed by women in groups.<br>• Tamil Nadu's other folk traditions include <b>Parai Attam, Karagattam, Oyilattam and Therukoothu</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विल्लुपाट्टु</b><br><b>विल्लुपाट्टु</b> <b>तमिलनाडु की आख्यान संगीत परंपरा</b> है, जिसमें घंटियों से युक्त बड़े <b>धनुषाकार वाद्य विल्लु</b> के साथ कथा सुनाई जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कलाकार डंडियों से धनुष की डोरी पर आघात करते हुए <b>रामायण, महाभारत तथा स्थानीय कथाएँ</b> सुनाते हैं।<br>• <b>यक्षगान</b> <b>कर्नाटक</b> का नृत्य-नाट्य रूप है तथा <b>ओप्पाना</b> <b>केरल के मुस्लिम समुदाय</b> का विवाह नृत्य है।<br>• <b>झूमर</b> <b>बंगाल, झारखंड तथा असम</b> की लोक नृत्य एवं गीत परंपरा है, जिसे महिलाएँ समूह में प्रस्तुत करती हैं।<br>• तमिलनाडु की अन्य लोक परंपराओं में <b>पराई आट्टम, करगाट्टम, ओयिलाट्टम तथा तेरुकूत्तु</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074730","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Sher Shah Suri is remembered for: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शेर शाह सूरी को किसके लिए याद किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Founding the Mansabdari system","hi":"मनसबदारी प्रथा की स्थापना"},"2":{"en":"Building the Grand Trunk Road & administrative reforms","hi":"ग्रैंड ट्रंक रोड का निर्माण तथा प्रशासनिक सुधार"},"3":{"en":"Construction of Fatehpur Sikri","hi":"फतेहपुर सीकरी का निर्माण"},"4":{"en":"Abolishing jizya","hi":"जजिया कर का उन्मूलन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Building the Grand Trunk Road & administrative reforms</b><br><b>Sher Shah Suri</b> is remembered for building the <b>Grand Trunk Road</b> from <b>Sonargaon in Bengal to Peshawar</b> and for wide-ranging <b>administrative reforms</b>, including the <b>ryotwari-like land revenue system</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He ruled from <b>1540 to 1545</b> after defeating Humayun at <b>Chausa and Kannauj</b> and introduced the <b>rupee</b> and the <b>sarais</b> (rest houses) along the road.<br>• His revenue system was based on <b>measurement of land and a schedule of rates</b>, later developed by Akbar's finance minister <b>Raja Todar Mal</b>.<br>• He built the <b>Purana Qila (Old Fort)</b> in Delhi and the <b>Sher Shah Suri Masjid</b> at Sasaram.<br>• The <b>Mansabdari system</b> was developed by <b>Akbar</b>, while the <b>jizya</b> was abolished by Akbar and later reimposed by Aurangzeb.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ग्रैंड ट्रंक रोड का निर्माण तथा प्रशासनिक सुधार</b><br><b>शेर शाह सूरी</b> को <b>बंगाल के सोनारगाँव से पेशावर</b> तक <b>ग्रैंड ट्रंक रोड</b> बनवाने तथा व्यापक <b>प्रशासनिक सुधारों</b>, जिनमें <b>रैयतवाड़ी जैसी भू-राजस्व व्यवस्था</b> शामिल है, के लिए याद किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उन्होंने <b>चौसा तथा कन्नौज</b> में हुमायूँ को पराजित करने के बाद <b>1540 से 1545</b> तक शासन किया और <b>रुपया</b> तथा मार्ग पर <b>सराय</b> (विश्रामगृह) आरंभ किए।<br>• उनकी राजस्व प्रणाली <b>भूमि मापन तथा दरों की सूची</b> पर आधारित थी, जिसे बाद में अकबर के वित्त मंत्री <b>राजा टोडरमल</b> ने विकसित किया।<br>• उन्होंने दिल्ली में <b>पुराना किला</b> तथा सासाराम में <b>शेर शाह सूरी मस्जिद</b> बनवाई।<br>• <b>मनसबदारी प्रणाली</b> <b>अकबर</b> ने विकसित की, जबकि <b>जजिया</b> अकबर ने समाप्त किया और औरंगजेब ने पुनः लगाया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074731","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A jacket, originally priced at ₹5,000, is sold with a 20% discount. The shopkeeper then faces two possibilities with the money he receives:<br>Possibility 1 (75% chance): He invests the money for 2 years at a 10% annual compound interest rate.<br>Possibility 2 (25% chance): He uses the money for other purposes, and it doesn't earn any interest.<br>Considering these possibilities and their likelihood, what is the average amount of money the shopkeeper can expect to have after 2 years as a result of this jacket sale? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"₹5,000 अंकित मूल्य वाली एक जैकेट 20% छूट पर बेची जाती है। इसके बाद दुकानदार को प्राप्त धन के संबंध में दो संभावनाएँ होती हैं:<br>संभावना 1 (75% संभावना): वह उस धन को 2 वर्ष के लिए 10% वार्षिक चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज दर पर निवेश करता है।<br>संभावना 2 (25% संभावना): वह उस धन का उपयोग अन्य कार्यों के लिए करता है और उस पर कोई ब्याज नहीं मिलता।<br>इन संभावनाओं और उनकी संभाव्यता को ध्यान में रखते हुए, इस जैकेट की बिक्री के परिणामस्वरूप दुकानदार 2 वर्ष बाद औसतन कितनी राशि रखने की अपेक्षा कर सकता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹4,430"},"2":{"en":"₹4,730"},"3":{"en":"₹4,530"},"4":{"en":"₹4,630"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Selling price = \\(5000 \\times \\frac{80}{100} = 4000\\)<br>Amount after 2 years at 10% CI = \\(4000 \\times 1.1^2 = 4840\\)<br>Expected amount = \\(4840 \\times \\frac{75}{100} + 4000 \\times \\frac{25}{100}\\)<br>\\(= 3630 + 1000 = \\boxed{4630}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹4,630.</b>","hi":"विक्रय मूल्य = \\(5000 \\times \\frac{80}{100} = 4000\\)<br>10% चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर 2 वर्ष बाद राशि = \\(4000 \\times 1.1^2 = 4840\\)<br>अपेक्षित राशि = \\(4840 \\times \\frac{75}{100} + 4000 \\times \\frac{25}{100}\\)<br>\\(= 3630 + 1000 = \\boxed{4630}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹4,630 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074732","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"In a right square pyramid, the length of a lateral edge is 20 cm. The height of the pyramid is 16 cm. Find the ratio of the slant height to the base side of the pyramid. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समकोणीय वर्गीय पिरामिड में एक पार्श्व किनारे की लंबाई 20 cm है। पिरामिड की ऊँचाई 16 cm है। पिरामिड की तिर्यक ऊँचाई (slant height) और आधार की भुजा का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{40}:16\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{41}:46\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{41}:6\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{41}:26\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M55 152H185L215 122H85Z\"/><path d=\"M135 35L55 152M135 35L185 152M135 35L215 122M135 35L85 122\"/><path d=\"M135 35V137\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M135 35L120 152\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M135 137L215 122\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M152 148H165M165 148V136\"/><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"137\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"35\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"146\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">16</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">16</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">20</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">20</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">l</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">l</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">a/2</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">a/2</text></g></svg><br>Let the base side be \\(a\\), half of it = \\(\\frac{a}{2}\\)<br>Half of the diagonal = \\(\\frac{a\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br>\\(\\left(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2 + 16^2 = 20^2 \\Rightarrow \\frac{a^2}{2} = 144 \\Rightarrow a = 12\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>Slant height \\(l = \\sqrt{16^2 + \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{256 + 72} = \\sqrt{328}\\)<br>\\(l : a = \\sqrt{328} : 12\\sqrt{2} = \\sqrt{41} : 6\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{6} = \\boxed{\\sqrt{41}:6}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\sqrt{41}:6\\).</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M55 152H185L215 122H85Z\"/><path d=\"M135 35L55 152M135 35L185 152M135 35L215 122M135 35L85 122\"/><path d=\"M135 35V137\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M135 35L120 152\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M135 137L215 122\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M152 148H165M165 148V136\"/><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"137\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"35\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"146\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">16</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">16</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">20</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">20</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">l</text><text x=\"104\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">l</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">a/2</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">a/2</text></g></svg><br>मान लीजिए आधार की भुजा \\(a\\) है, तो इसका आधा = \\(\\frac{a}{2}\\)<br>विकर्ण का आधा = \\(\\frac{a\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br>\\(\\left(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2 + 16^2 = 20^2 \\Rightarrow \\frac{a^2}{2} = 144 \\Rightarrow a = 12\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>तिर्यक ऊँचाई \\(l = \\sqrt{16^2 + \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{256 + 72} = \\sqrt{328}\\)<br>\\(l : a = \\sqrt{328} : 12\\sqrt{2} = \\sqrt{41} : 6\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{6} = \\boxed{\\sqrt{41}:6}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\sqrt{41}:6\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074733","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism with a pentagonal base has lateral surface area 900 cm². If the height is 15 cm, find the perimeter of the base. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पंचभुजीय आधार वाले एक लंब प्रिज़्म का पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 900 cm² है। यदि ऊँचाई 15 cm है, तो आधार का परिमाप ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"55 cm"},"2":{"en":"60 cm"},"3":{"en":"57 cm"},"4":{"en":"69 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 175\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M100 45L152.3 83L132.3 144.5L67.7 144.5L47.7 83Z\"/><path d=\"M150 15L202.3 53L182.3 114.5L117.7 114.5L97.7 53Z\"/><path d=\"M100 45L150 15M152.3 83L202.3 53M132.3 144.5L182.3 114.5M67.7 144.5L117.7 114.5M47.7 83L97.7 53\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">15 cm</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">15 cm</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">pentagonal base</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">pentagonal base</text></g></svg><br>Lateral surface area of a prism = perimeter of base × height<br>\\(900 = P \\times 15\\)<br>\\(P = \\frac{900}{15} = \\boxed{60}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 60 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 175\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M100 45L152.3 83L132.3 144.5L67.7 144.5L47.7 83Z\"/><path d=\"M150 15L202.3 53L182.3 114.5L117.7 114.5L97.7 53Z\"/><path d=\"M100 45L150 15M152.3 83L202.3 53M132.3 144.5L182.3 114.5M67.7 144.5L117.7 114.5M47.7 83L97.7 53\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">15 cm</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">15 cm</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">pentagonal base</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">pentagonal base</text></g></svg><br>प्रिज़्म का पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = आधार का परिमाप × ऊँचाई<br>\\(900 = P \\times 15\\)<br>\\(P = \\frac{900}{15} = \\boxed{60}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 60 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074734","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"The angle of elevation of the top of a tower from a point on the ground is 30°. If the height of the tower is 50m. Determine the distance from the point to the base of the tower. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भूमि पर एक बिंदु से किसी मीनार के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण 30° है। यदि मीनार की ऊँचाई 50m है, तो उस बिंदु से मीनार के आधार तक की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(25\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"2":{"en":"\\(50\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{50}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"100 m"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"235\" height=\"180\" viewBox=\"0 0 235 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M35 145H210\"/><path d=\"M60 145V45H68V145\"/><path d=\"M185 145L60 45\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">50 m</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">50 m</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30°</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30°</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"164\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">d = 50√3 m</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"164\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">d = 50√3 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{50}{d}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{50}{d}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{50\\sqrt{3}}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(50\\sqrt{3}\\) m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"235\" height=\"180\" viewBox=\"0 0 235 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M35 145H210\"/><path d=\"M60 145V45H68V145\"/><path d=\"M185 145L60 45\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">50 m</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">50 m</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30°</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30°</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"164\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">d = 50√3 m</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"164\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">d = 50√3 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{50}{d}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{50}{d}\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{50\\sqrt{3}}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(50\\sqrt{3}\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074735","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"Find the x-intercept of the line 5x−2y=10: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"रेखा 5x−2y=10 का x-अंतःखंड ज्ञात कीजिए: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"-2"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"x-intercept is obtained by putting \\(y = 0\\)<br>\\(5x - 2(0) = 10\\)<br>\\(x = \\frac{10}{5} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.</b>","hi":"x-अंतःखंड के लिए \\(y = 0\\) रखिए<br>\\(5x - 2(0) = 10\\)<br>\\(x = \\frac{10}{5} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074736","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Given below is the distribution of annual salaries (in thousands of INR) for 105 employees at a medium-sized company, answer the following questions based on this histogram.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019746bc-2499-757b-ba42-9b72bb19a9d5_EN.jpg?edu=639294378628500999\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What percentage of employees earn between ₹300,000 and ₹499,999?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019746bc-2499-757b-ba42-9b72bb19a9d5_EN.jpg?edu=639294378628500999\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे एक मध्यम आकार की कंपनी के 105 कर्मचारियों के वार्षिक वेतन (हज़ार INR में) का वितरण दिया गया है, इस हिस्टोग्राम के आधार पर निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों के उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019746bc-2499-757b-ba42-9b72bb19a9d5_HI.jpg?edu=639294378769704756\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>कितने प्रतिशत कर्मचारी ₹300,000 और ₹499,999 के बीच कमाते हैं?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019746bc-2499-757b-ba42-9b72bb19a9d5_HI.jpg?edu=639294378769704756\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50%"},"2":{"en":"60%"},"3":{"en":"57.14%"},"4":{"en":"80.67%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Salary (in ₹'000)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">200-299</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">300-399</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">400-499</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">500-599</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">600-699</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">700-799</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Employees</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr></table><br>Employees earning ₹300,000 to ₹499,999 = \\(25 + 35 = 60\\)<br>Total employees = 105<br>Required percentage = \\(\\frac{60}{105} \\times 100 = \\boxed{57.14}\\)%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 57.14%.</b>","hi":"<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">वेतन (₹'000 में)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">200-299</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">300-399</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">400-499</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">500-599</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">600-699</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">700-799</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">कर्मचारी</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr></table><br>₹300,000 से ₹499,999 कमाने वाले कर्मचारी = \\(25 + 35 = 60\\)<br>कुल कर्मचारी = 105<br>अभीष्ट प्रतिशत = \\(\\frac{60}{105} \\times 100 = \\boxed{57.14}\\)%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 57.14% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019746bc-2499-757b-ba42-9b72bb19a9d5_EN.jpg?edu=639294378628500999","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019746bc-2499-757b-ba42-9b72bb19a9d5_HI.jpg?edu=639294378769704756"]}},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074737","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Given below is the distribution of annual salaries (in thousands of INR) for 100 employees at a medium-sized company,answer the following questions based on this histogram.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019746be-362d-7efb-83f5-9781cd2b97f8_EN.jpg?edu=639294378628604294\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If 5 employees from the ₹400,000 - ₹499,999 range get promoted to the ₹500,000 - ₹599,999 range, what will be the new percentage of employees earning ₹500,000 or more?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019746be-362d-7efb-83f5-9781cd2b97f8_EN.jpg?edu=639294378628604294\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे एक मध्यम आकार की कंपनी के 100 कर्मचारियों के वार्षिक वेतन (हज़ार INR में) का वितरण दिया गया है, इस हिस्टोग्राम के आधार पर निम्नलिखित प्रश्नों के उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019746be-362d-7efb-83f5-9781cd2b97f8_HI.jpg?edu=639294378769787212\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि ₹400,000 - ₹499,999 श्रेणी के 5 कर्मचारियों को ₹500,000 - ₹599,999 श्रेणी में पदोन्नत किया जाए, तो ₹500,000 या अधिक कमाने वाले कर्मचारियों का नया प्रतिशत क्या होगा?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019746be-362d-7efb-83f5-9781cd2b97f8_HI.jpg?edu=639294378769787212\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"32.38%"},"2":{"en":"35.71%"},"3":{"en":"38.1%"},"4":{"en":"40%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From the histogram, employees earning ₹500,000 or more = \\(20 + 10 + 5 = 35\\)<br>After the promotion, 5 more employees enter this group = \\(35 + 5 = 40\\)<br>Total employees = 105<br>New percentage = \\(\\frac{40}{105} \\times 100 = \\boxed{38.1}\\)%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 38.1%.</b>","hi":"हिस्टोग्राम से, ₹500,000 या अधिक कमाने वाले कर्मचारी = \\(20 + 10 + 5 = 35\\)<br>पदोन्नति के बाद इस समूह में 5 और कर्मचारी जुड़ते हैं = \\(35 + 5 = 40\\)<br>कुल कर्मचारी = 105<br>नया प्रतिशत = \\(\\frac{40}{105} \\times 100 = \\boxed{38.1}\\)%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 38.1% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/EN/019746be-362d-7efb-83f5-9781cd2b97f8_EN.jpg?edu=639294378628604294","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct16/qimg/3/HI/019746be-362d-7efb-83f5-9781cd2b97f8_HI.jpg?edu=639294378769787212"]}},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074738","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Given (a + b)² = 25 and (a - b)² = 9, find a² - b². [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि (a + b)² = 25 और (a - b)² = 9 है, तो a² - b² ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"7"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\((a^2 - b^2)^2 = (a + b)^2(a - b)^2 = 25 \\times 9 = 225\\)<br>\\(a^2 - b^2 = \\sqrt{225} = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 15.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\((a^2 - b^2)^2 = (a + b)^2(a - b)^2 = 25 \\times 9 = 225\\)<br>\\(a^2 - b^2 = \\sqrt{225} = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074739","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If (x + y)³ = 27 and x - y = 1, find the value of xy. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि (x + y)³ = 27 और x - y = 1 है, तो xy का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x + y = 3\\) and \\(x - y = 1\\)<br>\\((x + y)^2 - (x - y)^2 = 4xy\\)<br>\\(9 - 1 = 4xy \\Rightarrow xy = \\frac{8}{4} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2.</b>","hi":"\\(x + y = 3\\) और \\(x - y = 1\\)<br>\\((x + y)^2 - (x - y)^2 = 4xy\\)<br>\\(9 - 1 = 4xy \\Rightarrow xy = \\frac{8}{4} = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074740","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A sum of ₹80,000 is invested at a compound interest rate of 7% per annum compounded quarterly.<br>What is the amount after 1 year? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"₹80,000 की राशि 7% वार्षिक चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज दर पर, जो प्रति तिमाही संयोजित होती है, निवेश की जाती है।<br>1 वर्ष बाद मिश्रधन क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"≈ ₹85,816.30"},"2":{"en":"≈ ₹85,600"},"3":{"en":"≈ ₹85,748.72"},"4":{"en":"≈ ₹85,900.62"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Quarterly rate = \\(\\frac{7}{4} = 1.75\\)%, quarters in 1 year = 4<br>Amount = \\(80000\\left(1 + \\frac{1.75}{100}\\right)^4 = 80000(1.0175)^4\\)<br>\\((1.0175)^4 = 1.071859\\)<br>Amount = \\(80000 \\times 1.071859 = \\boxed{85748.72}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ≈ ₹85,748.72.</b>","hi":"त्रैमासिक दर = \\(\\frac{7}{4} = 1.75\\)%, 1 वर्ष में तिमाहियाँ = 4<br>मिश्रधन = \\(80000\\left(1 + \\frac{1.75}{100}\\right)^4 = 80000(1.0175)^4\\)<br>\\((1.0175)^4 = 1.071859\\)<br>मिश्रधन = \\(80000 \\times 1.071859 = \\boxed{85748.72}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ≈ ₹85,748.72 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074741","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of length 10 cm is 6 cm away from the centre of a circle.<br>What is the radius of the circle? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"10 cm लंबाई की एक जीवा वृत्त के केंद्र से 6 cm दूर है।<br>वृत्त की त्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"√62 cm"},"2":{"en":"√63 cm"},"3":{"en":"√65 cm"},"4":{"en":"√61 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"78\"/><path d=\"M70 160H170\"/><path d=\"M120 100V160\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 100L170 160\"/><path d=\"M120 152H128V160\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">5</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">5</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">5</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">5</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r</text></g></svg><br>Half chord = \\(\\frac{10}{2} = 5\\) cm<br>Radius = \\(\\sqrt{6^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{61}}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): √61 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"78\"/><path d=\"M70 160H170\"/><path d=\"M120 100V160\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 100L170 160\"/><path d=\"M120 152H128V160\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">5</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">5</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">5</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"154\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">5</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r</text></g></svg><br>जीवा का आधा = \\(\\frac{10}{2} = 5\\) cm<br>त्रिज्या = \\(\\sqrt{6^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{61}}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): √61 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074742","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The distance between the centroid and the circumcentre of an equilateral triangle with a side of 6 cm is: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"6 cm भुजा वाले एक समबाहु त्रिभुज के केंद्रक और परिकेंद्र के बीच की दूरी है: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0 cm"},"2":{"en":"3 cm"},"3":{"en":"6 cm"},"4":{"en":"9 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"230\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M105 80L58 162H152Z\"/><path d=\"M105 80V162M58 162L128.5 121M152 162L81.5 121\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"134.7\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"141\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">G = O</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"141\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">G = O</text></g></svg><br>In an equilateral triangle the centroid, circumcentre, incentre and orthocentre all coincide.<br>Distance between centroid and circumcentre = \\(\\boxed{0}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 0 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"230\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M105 80L58 162H152Z\"/><path d=\"M105 80V162M58 162L128.5 121M152 162L81.5 121\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"134.7\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"48\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"141\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">G = O</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"141\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">G = O</text></g></svg><br>समबाहु त्रिभुज में केंद्रक, परिकेंद्र, अंतःकेंद्र और लंबकेंद्र सभी संपाती होते हैं।<br>केंद्रक और परिकेंद्र के बीच की दूरी = \\(\\boxed{0}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 0 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074743","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A square pyramid has a base edge of 5 cm and a height of 8 cm.<br>What is its volume in cubic cm? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वर्गीय पिरामिड के आधार की भुजा 5 cm और ऊँचाई 8 cm है।<br>इसका आयतन घन cm में क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"62.67"},"2":{"en":"64.67"},"3":{"en":"68"},"4":{"en":"66.67"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 152H170L195 127H85Z\"/><path d=\"M127.5 45L60 152M127.5 45L170 152M127.5 45L195 127M127.5 45L85 127\"/><path d=\"M127.5 45V139.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M140 139.5V152M140 139.5H152\"/><circle cx=\"127.5\" cy=\"139.5\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"127.5\" cy=\"45\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">5 cm</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">5 cm</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8 cm</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8 cm</text></g></svg><br>Volume of a pyramid = \\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times\\) base area × height<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 5^2 \\times 8 = \\frac{200}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{66.67}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 66.67.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 152H170L195 127H85Z\"/><path d=\"M127.5 45L60 152M127.5 45L170 152M127.5 45L195 127M127.5 45L85 127\"/><path d=\"M127.5 45V139.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M140 139.5V152M140 139.5H152\"/><circle cx=\"127.5\" cy=\"139.5\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"127.5\" cy=\"45\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">5 cm</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">5 cm</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8 cm</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8 cm</text></g></svg><br>पिरामिड का आयतन = \\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times\\) आधार क्षेत्रफल × ऊँचाई<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 5^2 \\times 8 = \\frac{200}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{66.67}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 66.67 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074744","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The radius of a cylinder is 10 cm and the height is 14 cm.<br>Find the curved surface area in square centimetres.<br>(Use π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बेलन की त्रिज्या 10 cm और ऊँचाई 14 cm है।<br>वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल वर्ग सेंटीमीटर में ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>(π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"880"},"2":{"en":"940"},"3":{"en":"900"},"4":{"en":"720"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><ellipse cx=\"120\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"15\"/><path d=\"M65 50V150M175 50V150\"/><path d=\"M65 150a55 15 0 0 0 110 0\"/><path d=\"M65 150a55 15 0 0 1 110 0\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 50H155\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"50\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h = 14</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h = 14</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 10</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 10</text></g></svg><br>Curved surface area = \\(2\\pi r h\\)<br>\\(= 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 10 \\times 14\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{880}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 880.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><ellipse cx=\"120\" cy=\"50\" rx=\"55\" ry=\"15\"/><path d=\"M65 50V150M175 50V150\"/><path d=\"M65 150a55 15 0 0 0 110 0\"/><path d=\"M65 150a55 15 0 0 1 110 0\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 50H155\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"50\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h = 14</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h = 14</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 10</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 10</text></g></svg><br>वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(2\\pi r h\\)<br>\\(= 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 10 \\times 14\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{880}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 880 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074745","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"A village health centre recorded the number of patients attending over six days in a bar diagram: 120, 150, 130, 140, 110, and 160.<br>Based on this data, what is the average number of patients per day? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक गाँव के स्वास्थ्य केंद्र ने छह दिनों में आने वाले रोगियों की संख्या बार आरेख में दर्ज की: 120, 150, 130, 140, 110 और 160।<br>इस आँकड़े के आधार पर प्रति दिन रोगियों की औसत संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"145"},"2":{"en":"140"},"3":{"en":"135"},"4":{"en":"130"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Total patients = \\(120 + 150 + 130 + 140 + 110 + 160 = 810\\)<br>Average = \\(\\frac{810}{6}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{135}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 135.</b>","hi":"कुल रोगी = \\(120 + 150 + 130 + 140 + 110 + 160 = 810\\)<br>औसत = \\(\\frac{810}{6}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{135}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 135 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074746","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"A pie chart represents the sales of 4 different crops in a village.<br>If the angle for wheat is 108°, what fraction of total sales does wheat represent? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक पाई चार्ट किसी गाँव में 4 भिन्न फसलों की बिक्री को दर्शाता है।<br>यदि गेहूँ के लिए कोण 108° है, तो गेहूँ कुल बिक्री का कितना भाग दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3/10"},"2":{"en":"3/8"},"3":{"en":"3/7"},"4":{"en":"3/5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Fraction of total sales = \\(\\frac{\\text{angle}}{360^\\circ}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{108}{360} = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{10}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3/10.</b>","hi":"कुल बिक्री का भाग = \\(\\frac{\\text{कोण}}{360^\\circ}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{108}{360} = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{10}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3/10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074747","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cosθ = 1, what is sin²θ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि cosθ = 1 है, तो sin²θ क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"0"},"4":{"en":"-1"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - 1^2 = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 0.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - 1^2 = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074748","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"A student notes tanθ = 3/4.<br>What is the value of sec²θ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक विद्यार्थी tanθ = 3/4 नोट करता है।<br>sec²θ का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25/16"},"2":{"en":"11/25"},"3":{"en":"16/25"},"4":{"en":"9/25"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + \\tan^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 + \\frac{9}{16}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{25}{16}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 25/16.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + \\tan^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 + \\frac{9}{16}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{25}{16}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 25/16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074749","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"It is given that sinθ = 3/5.<br>If θ is acute, find cos²θ. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यह दिया गया है कि sinθ = 3/5 है।<br>यदि θ न्यून कोण है, तो cos²θ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16/25"},"2":{"en":"18/25"},"3":{"en":"25/16"},"4":{"en":"14/25"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - \\frac{9}{25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{16}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 16/25.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - \\sin^2\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - \\frac{9}{25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{16}{25}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 16/25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074750","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"A library has 1521 books. The librarian arranges them equally on square racks.<br>How many books should be on each side of a square rack? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक पुस्तकालय में 1521 पुस्तकें हैं। पुस्तकालयाध्यक्ष उन्हें वर्गाकार रैक पर समान रूप से व्यवस्थित करता है।<br>एक वर्गाकार रैक की प्रत्येक भुजा पर कितनी पुस्तकें होनी चाहिए? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"41"},"2":{"en":"31"},"3":{"en":"49"},"4":{"en":"39"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"For a square rack, books on each side = \\(\\sqrt{1521}\\)<br>\\(40^2 = 1600\\), so the answer is a little less than 40<br>\\(39 \\times 39 = 1521\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{39}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 39.</b>","hi":"वर्गाकार रैक के लिए, प्रत्येक भुजा पर पुस्तकें = \\(\\sqrt{1521}\\)<br>\\(40^2 = 1600\\), अतः उत्तर 40 से कुछ कम है<br>\\(39 \\times 39 = 1521\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{39}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 39 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074751","section":"MATH","topic":"Problems on Trains","question":{"en":"A 240 m long train passes a man walking at 6 km/h in the opposite direction in 12 seconds.<br>Find the train's speed. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"240 m लंबी एक ट्रेन विपरीत दिशा में 6 km/h की चाल से चल रहे एक व्यक्ति को 12 सेकंड में पार करती है।<br>ट्रेन की चाल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"60 km/h"},"2":{"en":"62 km/h"},"3":{"en":"66 km/h"},"4":{"en":"72 km/h"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 170\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><rect x=\"35\" y=\"65\" width=\"140\" height=\"45\" rx=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"57\" cy=\"117\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"117\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"147\" cy=\"117\" r=\"7\"/><path d=\"M55 48H145M139 42L145 48L139 54\"/><circle cx=\"222\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\"/><path d=\"M222 66V90M222 90L214 106M222 90L230 106M222 74L211 84M222 74L233 84\"/><path d=\"M252 34H208M214 28L208 34L214 40\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">240 m</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">240 m</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">train</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">train</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6 km/h</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6 km/h</text></g></svg><br>Relative speed (opposite direction) = \\(\\frac{240}{12} = 20\\) m/s<br>\\(20 \\times \\frac{18}{5} = 72\\) km/h<br>Train's speed = \\(72 - 6 = \\boxed{66}\\) km/h<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 66 km/h.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 170\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><rect x=\"35\" y=\"65\" width=\"140\" height=\"45\" rx=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"57\" cy=\"117\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"117\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"147\" cy=\"117\" r=\"7\"/><path d=\"M55 48H145M139 42L145 48L139 54\"/><circle cx=\"222\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\"/><path d=\"M222 66V90M222 90L214 106M222 90L230 106M222 74L211 84M222 74L233 84\"/><path d=\"M252 34H208M214 28L208 34L214 40\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">240 m</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">240 m</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">train</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">train</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6 km/h</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6 km/h</text></g></svg><br>सापेक्ष चाल (विपरीत दिशा) = \\(\\frac{240}{12} = 20\\) m/s<br>\\(20 \\times \\frac{18}{5} = 72\\) km/h<br>ट्रेन की चाल = \\(72 - 6 = \\boxed{66}\\) km/h<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 66 km/h है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074752","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A job is completed by 3 workers in 12 days.<br>How many days will it take for 9 workers to complete the same job? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक कार्य 3 मज़दूरों द्वारा 12 दिनों में पूरा होता है।<br>उसी कार्य को 9 मज़दूर कितने दिनों में पूरा करेंगे? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 days","hi":"6 दिन"},"2":{"en":"3 days","hi":"3 दिन"},"3":{"en":"4 days","hi":"4 दिन"},"4":{"en":"5 days","hi":"5 दिन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Work = \\(3 \\times 12 = 36\\) man-days<br>Days for 9 workers = \\(\\frac{36}{9}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4 days.</b>","hi":"कार्य = \\(3 \\times 12 = 36\\) मज़दूर-दिन<br>9 मज़दूरों के लिए दिन = \\(\\frac{36}{9}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4}\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074753","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A typist can type 30 pages in 6 hours.<br>How many pages can 4 typists type in 3 hours, assuming uniform speed? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक टाइपिस्ट 6 घंटे में 30 पृष्ठ टाइप कर सकता है।<br>समान गति मानते हुए, 4 टाइपिस्ट 3 घंटे में कितने पृष्ठ टाइप कर सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70"},"2":{"en":"90"},"3":{"en":"80"},"4":{"en":"60"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Pages typed by 1 typist in 1 hour = \\(\\frac{30}{6} = 5\\)<br>Pages by 4 typists in 3 hours = \\(5 \\times 4 \\times 3\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{60}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 60.</b>","hi":"1 टाइपिस्ट 1 घंटे में पृष्ठ टाइप करता है = \\(\\frac{30}{6} = 5\\)<br>4 टाइपिस्ट 3 घंटे में पृष्ठ टाइप करेंगे = \\(5 \\times 4 \\times 3\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{60}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 60 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074754","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper reduces the price from ₹12.75 to ₹9.6. What is the exact discount in rupees? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकानदार मूल्य ₹12.75 से घटाकर ₹9.6 कर देता है। रुपयों में ठीक छूट कितनी है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3.05"},"2":{"en":"₹3.15"},"3":{"en":"₹3.25"},"4":{"en":"₹3.1"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Discount = \\(12.75 - 9.60\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3.15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹3.15.</b>","hi":"छूट = \\(12.75 - 9.60\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3.15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹3.15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074755","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper mixes 20 kg of sugar at Rs. 30/kg with 40 kg at Rs. 50/kg. Find the price per kg of the mixture. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकानदार 20 kg चीनी Rs. 30/kg पर 40 kg चीनी Rs. 50/kg के साथ मिलाता है। मिश्रण का प्रति kg मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"43.33"},"2":{"en":"40"},"3":{"en":"42"},"4":{"en":"44"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Total cost = \\(20 \\times 30 + 40 \\times 50 = 600 + 2000 = 2600\\)<br>Total quantity = \\(20 + 40 = 60\\) kg<br>Price per kg = \\(\\frac{2600}{60} = \\boxed{43.33}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 43.33.</b>","hi":"कुल लागत = \\(20 \\times 30 + 40 \\times 50 = 600 + 2000 = 2600\\)<br>कुल मात्रा = \\(20 + 40 = 60\\) kg<br>प्रति kg मूल्य = \\(\\frac{2600}{60} = \\boxed{43.33}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 43.33 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074756","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Benevolent</b> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Charitable"},"2":{"en":"Kind"},"3":{"en":"Cruel"},"4":{"en":"Gentle"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Benevolent (परोपकारी) = kind and generous.</b><br><b>Charitable (दानशील)</b> = generous<br><b>Kind (दयालु)</b> = caring<br><b>Cruel (क्रूर)</b> = deliberately causing suffering ✔<br><b>Gentle (कोमल)</b> = mild and kind; other antonyms: malevolent, unkind.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Cruel.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074757","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Choose the sentence containing the homonym of the underlined word:<br>He couldn't <b>bear</b> the pain. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The bear was wandering in the forest."},"2":{"en":"She couldn't bear the noise."},"3":{"en":"He couldn't bear the loss."},"4":{"en":"Bear with me for a moment."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Bear (सहना) = endure; bear (भालू) = the animal.</b><br>The original uses the verb meaning “endure.”<br>Option A uses the noun naming the animal.<br>The other options use the verb meaning endure or tolerate.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The bear was wandering in the forest..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074758","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the below given indirect speech into direct speech appropriately:<br>He said that he was watching a movie. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He said, “I will watch a movie”."},"2":{"en":"He said, “I watch a movie”."},"3":{"en":"He said, “I have watched a movie”."},"4":{"en":"He said, “I am watching a movie”."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past continuous reverses to present continuous in direct speech.</b><br>“Was watching” becomes “am watching.”<br>The reported “he” returns to “I.”<br>The other options use incompatible tenses.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): He said, “I am watching a movie”..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074759","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Identify the option that best corrects the highlighted part of the sentence for proper grammar and usage.<br>She succeeded <b>in win</b> the competition. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"for win"},"2":{"en":"in winning"},"3":{"en":"of winning"},"4":{"en":"with winning"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Succeed in + gerund” is the standard construction.</b><br>Correct sentence: “She succeeded <b>in winning</b> the competition.”<br>The preposition “in” must be followed by “winning.”<br>The other prepositions do not fit the idiom.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): in winning.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074760","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Identify the option that best corrects the highlighted part of the sentence for proper grammar and usage.<br>She <b>insisted to go</b> to the market. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"insisted to going"},"2":{"en":"insisted on going"},"3":{"en":"insisted going"},"4":{"en":"insisted with going"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Insist on + gerund” is the standard construction.</b><br>Correct sentence: “She <b>insisted on going</b> to the market.”<br>“To going” and “with going” are unidiomatic.<br>The preposition “on” cannot be omitted here.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): insisted on going.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074761","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Spot the error in the following sentence and identify the INCORRECT part.<br>I have been waiting <b>since two hours</b> for the bus. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"have been waiting"},"2":{"en":"since two hours"},"3":{"en":"for the bus"},"4":{"en":"No error"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use “for” with a duration and “since” with a starting point.</b><br>“Two hours” is a duration, so use “for two hours.”<br>“Since” would require a point such as “since 8 a.m.”<br>The erroneous phrase is “since two hours.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): since two hours.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074762","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Spot the error in the following sentence and identify the INCORRECT part.<br>She is <b>good with mathematics</b> but weak in physics. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"No error"},"2":{"en":"but weak"},"3":{"en":"good with mathematics"},"4":{"en":"in physics"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The idiomatic adjective–preposition pair is “good at mathematics.”</b><br>“Good with” generally refers to handling people or things.<br>“Weak in physics” is acceptable.<br>The erroneous phrase is “good with mathematics.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): good with mathematics.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074763","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Identify the odd one: which of the following words does not belong to the group? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pugilist"},"2":{"en":"Fencer"},"3":{"en":"Boxer"},"4":{"en":"Pacifist"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Pacifist (शांतिवादी) = a person opposed to war and violence.</b><br><b>Pugilist</b> and <b>boxer</b> both mean a person who fights with fists.<br>A <b>fencer</b> practices sword fighting as a sport.<br>The pacifist is the odd one out.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Pacifist.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074764","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"What is the antonym of the word “ostensible”? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Depressed"},"2":{"en":"Real"},"3":{"en":"Illogical"},"4":{"en":"Unpredictable"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Ostensible (प्रकट/दिखावटी) = appearing true but not necessarily actual.</b><br><b>Real (वास्तविक)</b> = genuine or actual ✔<br><b>Depressed (उदास)</b> = sad<br><b>Illogical (अतार्किक)</b> = unreasonable; <b>unpredictable (अप्रत्याशित)</b> = uncertain.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Real.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074765","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Pay through the nose” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Get a big discount"},"2":{"en":"Pay much more than usual"},"3":{"en":"Borrow money from a friend"},"4":{"en":"Avoid paying altogether"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Pay through the nose (बहुत अधिक भुगतान करना) = pay an exorbitant amount.</b><br>Example: “We paid through the nose for last-minute tickets.”<br>Discounts, borrowing and avoiding payment are unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Pay much more than usual.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074766","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“The powers that be” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Supernatural forces"},"2":{"en":"Current authorities"},"3":{"en":"Past rulers"},"4":{"en":"Media groups"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>The powers that be (सत्ता में बैठे लोग) = those currently in authority.</b><br>Example: “The powers that be have postponed the decision.”<br>The phrase does not specifically mean supernatural forces, past rulers or media.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Current authorities.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074767","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>His consistent refusal to acknowledge empirical evidence reflects a dangerous ___ to ideological rigidity. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"adherence"},"2":{"en":"resistance"},"3":{"en":"deference"},"4":{"en":"contribution"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Adherence (अनुपालन) = firm attachment to a belief or practice.</b><br>“Adherence to ideological rigidity” fits the refusal to consider evidence.<br>“Resistance to” would mean opposition, reversing the meaning.<br>Deference and contribution do not fit the context.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): adherence.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074768","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the correctly spelt word which means a detailed plan or schedule of a trip, listing the places to visit, activities, and times for each part of the journey. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Itenary"},"2":{"en":"Iteniry"},"3":{"en":"Itinerery"},"4":{"en":"Itinerary"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Itinerary (यात्रा-कार्यक्रम) = a detailed travel plan.</b><br>The correct spelling is “itinerary.”<br><b>Itenary</b> omits “i” and “r”; <b>iteniry</b> has additional omissions.<br><b>Itinerery</b> incorrectly uses “e” before “ry.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Itinerary.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074769","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.<br>“No sooner had he stepped outside than the alarm went off,” said the guard. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The guard said that as soon as he had stepped outside, the alarm had gone off."},"2":{"en":"The guard said that no sooner had he stepped outside than the alarm went off."},"3":{"en":"The guard said no sooner he stepped outside than the alarm had gone off."},"4":{"en":"The guard said the moment he stepped outside, the alarm had gone off."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The correlative structure “no sooner … than” may be retained in reported speech.</b><br>“Had he stepped” is past perfect, and “went off” remains past in the keyed construction.<br>A unnecessarily replaces the structure and backshifts both clauses.<br>C and D remove the required inversion or alter the original structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The guard said that no sooner had he stepped outside than the alarm went off..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074770","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. A list of shortlisted candidates is published.<br>2. Applications are screened.<br>3. Interviews are scheduled.<br>4. Selected candidates are emailed. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-4-3-1"},"2":{"en":"1-2-3-4"},"3":{"en":"3-1-2-4"},"4":{"en":"2-1-3-4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-3-4</b><br>Applications are screened before the shortlist is published.<br>Interviews are then scheduled.<br>Selected candidates are emailed last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2-1-3-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074771","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P. were introduced as part of the digital governance reform<br>Q. biometric attendance systems<br>R. to reduce proxy attendance and data manipulation<br>S. across all urban local bodies [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRPS"},"2":{"en":"QPRS"},"3":{"en":"RQPS"},"4":{"en":"RSPQ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QPRS</b><br>Q supplies the subject, and P gives the passive predicate.<br>R states the purpose of biometric attendance.<br>S identifies the institutions where the systems were introduced.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QPRS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074772","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P. were subjected to scrutiny by audit authorities<br>Q. for inconsistencies in declared financial holdings<br>R. senior administrative officers<br>S. across multiple state departments [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RSQP"},"2":{"en":"RQSP"},"3":{"en":"RPSQ"},"4":{"en":"QPRS"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPSQ</b><br>R supplies the subject, and P supplies the passive predicate.<br>S locates the officers across state departments.<br>Q explains the reason for the scrutiny.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): QPRS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074773","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>In the aftermath of collective trauma, societies instinctively reach for narrative closure, mistaking coherence for truth. This need to structure experience often leads to the (1)___ of complex realities into simplified myths. While such narratives may offer solace, they frequently occlude the structural forces that made the crisis possible. Memory, in these moments, is less an archive than a battleground—a terrain where meaning is not discovered but contested. Cultural institutions, instead of resisting this flattening, often become its architects, prioritizing commemorative spectacle over analytical excavation. The result is a politics of memory shaped more by utility than by integrity. What emerges is not a history, but a curated (2)___, designed to domesticate discomfort. In this framework, dissent is not persecuted, but anesthetized—absorbed and neutralized through symbolic inclusion. Such strategies manufacture a sense of reconciliation while leaving the epistemic violence untouched. To resist this drift requires an (3)___ commitment to confronting discomfort without prematurely resolving it. Societies must learn to inhabit ambiguity without succumbing to paralysis. Otherwise, public memory will continue to be governed by what is palatable, not what is (4)___, and truth will become a function not of verification but of narrative (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 1? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ossification"},"2":{"en":"distillation"},"3":{"en":"subversion"},"4":{"en":"transposition"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Distillation (संक्षेपण) = reduction to essential or simplified elements.</b><br>Complex realities are distilled into simplified myths.<br><b>Ossification (कठोरीकरण)</b> = becoming rigid<br><b>Subversion (विध्वंस)</b> = undermining; <b>transposition (अदल-बदल)</b> = changing order<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): distillation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074774","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P: of community-oriented justice<br>Q: modern legal systems<br>R: often marginalise<br>S: the embedded practices [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QSRP"},"2":{"en":"QSPR"},"3":{"en":"QRSP"},"4":{"en":"RPQS"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q supplies the subject, and R the verb “often marginalise.”<br>S supplies the object: the embedded practices.<br>P completes the object as practices of community-oriented justice.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074775","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>In the aftermath of collective trauma, societies instinctively reach for narrative closure, mistaking coherence for truth. This need to structure experience often leads to the (1)___ of complex realities into simplified myths. While such narratives may offer solace, they frequently occlude the structural forces that made the crisis possible. Memory, in these moments, is less an archive than a battleground—a terrain where meaning is not discovered but contested. Cultural institutions, instead of resisting this flattening, often become its architects, prioritizing commemorative spectacle over analytical excavation. The result is a politics of memory shaped more by utility than by integrity. What emerges is not a history, but a curated (2)___, designed to domesticate discomfort. In this framework, dissent is not persecuted, but anesthetized—absorbed and neutralized through symbolic inclusion. Such strategies manufacture a sense of reconciliation while leaving the epistemic violence untouched. To resist this drift requires an (3)___ commitment to confronting discomfort without prematurely resolving it. Societies must learn to inhabit ambiguity without succumbing to paralysis. Otherwise, public memory will continue to be governed by what is palatable, not what is (4)___, and truth will become a function not of verification but of narrative (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 2? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"mnemonic"},"2":{"en":"palimpsest"},"3":{"en":"artifact"},"4":{"en":"dramaturgy"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Dramaturgy (नाटकीय प्रस्तुति) = the crafted presentation of a narrative or spectacle.</b><br>A curated dramaturgy domesticates discomfort through symbolic presentation.<br><b>Mnemonic (स्मृति-सहायक)</b> = memory aid<br><b>Palimpsest</b> = reused surface bearing traces; <b>artifact</b> = human-made object<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): dramaturgy.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074776","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>In the aftermath of collective trauma, societies instinctively reach for narrative closure, mistaking coherence for truth. This need to structure experience often leads to the (1)___ of complex realities into simplified myths. While such narratives may offer solace, they frequently occlude the structural forces that made the crisis possible. Memory, in these moments, is less an archive than a battleground—a terrain where meaning is not discovered but contested. Cultural institutions, instead of resisting this flattening, often become its architects, prioritizing commemorative spectacle over analytical excavation. The result is a politics of memory shaped more by utility than by integrity. What emerges is not a history, but a curated (2)___, designed to domesticate discomfort. In this framework, dissent is not persecuted, but anesthetized—absorbed and neutralized through symbolic inclusion. Such strategies manufacture a sense of reconciliation while leaving the epistemic violence untouched. To resist this drift requires an (3)___ commitment to confronting discomfort without prematurely resolving it. Societies must learn to inhabit ambiguity without succumbing to paralysis. Otherwise, public memory will continue to be governed by what is palatable, not what is (4)___, and truth will become a function not of verification but of narrative (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 3? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ascetic"},"2":{"en":"unflinching"},"3":{"en":"forensic"},"4":{"en":"dogmatic"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Unflinching (अडिग) = resolute and unafraid.</b><br>Confronting discomfort without resolving it prematurely requires an unflinching commitment.<br><b>Ascetic (तपस्वी)</b> = severely self-disciplined<br><b>Forensic (न्यायालयीन)</b> = investigative; <b>dogmatic (कट्टर)</b> = rigidly opinionated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): unflinching.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074777","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>In the aftermath of collective trauma, societies instinctively reach for narrative closure, mistaking coherence for truth. This need to structure experience often leads to the (1)___ of complex realities into simplified myths. While such narratives may offer solace, they frequently occlude the structural forces that made the crisis possible. Memory, in these moments, is less an archive than a battleground—a terrain where meaning is not discovered but contested. Cultural institutions, instead of resisting this flattening, often become its architects, prioritizing commemorative spectacle over analytical excavation. The result is a politics of memory shaped more by utility than by integrity. What emerges is not a history, but a curated (2)___, designed to domesticate discomfort. In this framework, dissent is not persecuted, but anesthetized—absorbed and neutralized through symbolic inclusion. Such strategies manufacture a sense of reconciliation while leaving the epistemic violence untouched. To resist this drift requires an (3)___ commitment to confronting discomfort without prematurely resolving it. Societies must learn to inhabit ambiguity without succumbing to paralysis. Otherwise, public memory will continue to be governed by what is palatable, not what is (4)___, and truth will become a function not of verification but of narrative (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 4? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"methodical"},"2":{"en":"subaltern"},"3":{"en":"dissonant"},"4":{"en":"indispensable"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Dissonant (विसंगत) = clashing or discordant.</b><br>Public memory prefers what is palatable rather than dissonant or disturbing.<br><b>Methodical (सुव्यवस्थित)</b> = systematic<br><b>Subaltern (अधीनस्थ)</b> = subordinate; <b>indispensable (अपरिहार्य)</b> = essential<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): dissonant.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074778","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the passage below, certain words have been removed. Read the passage thoroughly and choose the most suitable option to complete each blank appropriately.<br><br>In the aftermath of collective trauma, societies instinctively reach for narrative closure, mistaking coherence for truth. This need to structure experience often leads to the (1)___ of complex realities into simplified myths. While such narratives may offer solace, they frequently occlude the structural forces that made the crisis possible. Memory, in these moments, is less an archive than a battleground—a terrain where meaning is not discovered but contested. Cultural institutions, instead of resisting this flattening, often become its architects, prioritizing commemorative spectacle over analytical excavation. The result is a politics of memory shaped more by utility than by integrity. What emerges is not a history, but a curated (2)___, designed to domesticate discomfort. In this framework, dissent is not persecuted, but anesthetized—absorbed and neutralized through symbolic inclusion. Such strategies manufacture a sense of reconciliation while leaving the epistemic violence untouched. To resist this drift requires an (3)___ commitment to confronting discomfort without prematurely resolving it. Societies must learn to inhabit ambiguity without succumbing to paralysis. Otherwise, public memory will continue to be governed by what is palatable, not what is (4)___, and truth will become a function not of verification but of narrative (5)___.<br><br><br>What should come in the place of blank number 5? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"circulation"},"2":{"en":"coherence"},"3":{"en":"repetition"},"4":{"en":"curation"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Coherence (सुसंगतता) = logical consistency.</b><br>The opening warns that societies mistake coherence for truth; the ending returns to that idea.<br>Truth becomes a function of narrative coherence rather than verification.<br>Circulation, repetition and curation do not complete this deliberate echo as precisely.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): coherence.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074779","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P: in legitimising state violence<br>Q: under regimes of legal formalism<br>R: the abstraction of rule of law<br>S: often functions [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRPS"},"2":{"en":"RSPQ"},"3":{"en":"RQSP"},"4":{"en":"QSRP"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RSPQ</b><br>R supplies the subject: the abstraction of rule of law.<br>S gives the verb “often functions.”<br>P explains its function, and Q supplies the governing context.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RSPQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074780","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct option to rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph:<br>B. They were calling out to him loudly.<br>A. He lowered his legs to land on the green sea.<br>C. His parents, brothers, and sister had landed ahead on the green surface.<br>D. But his legs sank into the water. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"CBAD"},"2":{"en":"CBDA"},"3":{"en":"ADCB"},"4":{"en":"ABCD"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: CBAD</b><br>C introduces the family members already on the green surface.<br>B says they called to him, and A describes his attempt to land.<br>D gives the unexpected result: his legs sank into the water.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): CBAD.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};